29`, then resolved against the session cwd). The receipt records `workspace` and `base_pinned_at`, but the `_nexus/verify` result does not name the workspace. Add it to the result and document the behaviour.\n3. **Id-less `_nexus/receipt/get` can return a verification receipt** (confirmed by running; `latestReceipts`, about lines 353 and 418). The plan said id-less get keeps returning turn receipts only, so existing clients see no change. The test near `acp_stdio.test.ts:118` asserts the mixed behaviour.\n4. **Interlocks are untested.** Removing the \"no verify during a prompt\" check leaves `acp_stdio` (9/9) and `acp_review_fixes` (8/8) green. There is no test for verify during a prompt or a stopping turn, a prompt during a verify, or read-only refusal over ACP; the cross-session receipt test (about line 125) uses a session id that is not active.\n5. **Shutdown bound.** `ACP_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_MS` (10 s) equals the verify kill grace, so on a signal the process can exit before the worker has removed its scratch trees. `serve-mcp` allows 15 s. By reading only.\n6. `_meta` is accepted on `_nexus/verify` and ignored; the docs say nothing else is accepted.\n\n**Mutations run:** accepting an extra param fails `acp_stdio` and `acp_validate`; dropping the receipt's session binding fails `acp_stdio` and `verify_service`; allowing verify during a prompt fails nothing (item 4).\n\n**Tests at `f25030a3`, 0 failures:** `acp_stdio` 9, `acp_validate` 15, `acp_schema` 7, `acp_mapping` 22, `acp_review_fixes` 8, `acp_client_conformance` 2, `verify_service` 10, `mcp_verify` 7, `mcp` 4.\n\n**Not checked:** the real adapter over stdio with a real worker, SIGTERM of `nexus acp` during a live verification, two verifications on two sessions, Node 22.\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChLcZ7fTJCpZpCGvFH5dN","requestRef":"f645dc8c-d4b5-4c29-9fd8-756062409fc7","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"0830cefd-7fe2-45f1-a9d5-cd9ae2f0cf1d"