{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-23T22:32:41.804Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a3c546d665613d240</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_018E5VP5zBeYJcoQgHV8TTpV</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/a3c546d665613d240.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Review PR #760 inference budget\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>**Verdict: REQUEST CHANGES** at `75a838be1a3d73c4eeda0224a65d86d0c9f63735`. The head did not move between the start and the end of the review.\n\n**Findings**\n\n1. **Blocking, confirmed by running.** `cli/test/protocol_parity.test.ts` fails at head (\"checked-in schema samples equal a fresh generation\") and passes 5/5 on `origin/release/v1.3.0`.\n   - The PR changed `sidecar-v1.schema.json` but did not regenerate `cli/test/fixtures/protocol_v1_schema_samples.jsonl`. The `history` full sample lacks `inferenceSubmissions`, `maxInferenceSubmissions` and `inferenceSubmissionHistoryComplete`.\n   - Fix: run `node cli/scripts/gen_protocol_samples.mjs` and commit the fixture. The Rust parity test reads the same fixture, so check that too.\n\n2. **Non-blocking, by reading.** The bound is not aggregate over all inference.\n   - Only the primary turn loop is counted, at `run_turn.ts:~692`, via `beforeSubmit` and `reserveInferenceSubmission` (`run_turn.ts:263`).\n   - The docs (`COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md`) and the plan progress note state that subagents and durable operation units are not counted.\n   - They do not state that three side calls are also uncounted: findings extraction (`agent.ts:3307`), the compaction probe (`agent.ts:3758`) and the compaction summary (`agent.ts:3797`). Each sends a model request. \"Covers the primary objective turn\" is ambiguous about them.\n   - Fix: list them as uncounted, or count them.\n\n3. **Non-blocking, by reading.** The project `.env` can raise the budget. `NEXUS_MAX_INFERENCE_SUBMISSIONS` is in `PROJECT_ENV_KEYS` (`config.ts:188`). A repository can therefore move a new objective's ceiling from 1,000 to 10,000. This matches the existing `NEXUS_MAX_TOOL_INVOCATIONS` precedent, but the docs never say a project can set it. A raise on resume is blocked, because `Math.min(saved, configured)` is used at `run_turn.ts:~193`.\n\n4. **Non-blocking, by reading.** The non-durable path (`!this.durable`) uses `ExecutionTracker.fresh()` (`run_turn.ts:160`). The counter is per-turn there, with no persistence, and the docs do not say so.\n\n**Answers to the questions**\n\n- **Limit behaviour:** the turn ends with `execution=LIMIT_REACHED`, reason `INFERENCE_SUBMISSION_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED`, outcome `NOT_ESTABLISHED`. This is never COMPLETED or VERIFIED.\n- **Retry at the limit:** a denied retry moves the recovery record to `EXHAUSTED` and rethrows. Nothing retries afterwards.\n- **Boundary:** `min(1, max - count)` allows exactly N submissions. The test confirms 1/1 sends exactly one request.\n- **Persistence:** the reservation is saved before dispatch, and a save failure sends no request. A malformed counter or ceiling throws before any inference. Legacy records report their earlier history as unknown.\n- **Config:** invalid values throw (fail-closed), with a minimum of 1, a default of 1,000 and a maximum of 10,000. I found no tool call or model path that sets the value.\n- **Policy:** `policy_runtime.ts` has no tool-invocation clamp to mirror, and the PR does not touch policy or approval code. Nothing is loosened by reading. I did not exercise this.\n- **Protocol:** the change is additive. Only new entries were appended to `RUN_RESULT_VERSIONS.json` and `VERSIONS.json`, and `schema_version` stays 1. The tests `run_json_contract` and `protocol_schema` pass. The doctor config key is consistent.\n\n**Submission paths**\n\n| Path | Counted |\n|---|---|\n| Main turn loop | yes |\n| Provider-recovery retries | yes |\n| Resume of a durable objective | yes (persisted, can only be lowered) |\n| Continuation segments | yes (same tracker) |\n| Alternate-provider selection | yes (only the primary-loop submit hook is counted) |\n| Subagent loop (`agent.ts:4743`) | no, documented |\n| Operation runner | no, documented |\n| Compaction summary and probe | no, not documented |\n| Findings extraction | no, not documented |\n| Worktrunk commit message | no |\n| `doctor` and `provider_cli` diagnostics | no |\n| Availability probes | no, documented |\n\n**Mutations** (each reverted with `git checkout`)\n\nAll three made the new test file fail: 3 passed and 1 failed each time, the failure being the retry/resume test.\n- (a) Admission check disabled.\n- (b) Retries not counted (`attempt &gt; 1` skipped).\n- (c) Counter reset to 0 on resume.\n\nThe tests exercise only a limit of 1.\n\n**Test counts**\n\n| File | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `p10_inference_submission_budget` | 4/4 pass |\n| `run_json_contract` | 15 pass, 0 fail |\n| `protocol_schema` | 8 pass, 0 fail |\n| `context_convergence` | 57 pass, 0 fail |\n| `protocol_parity` | 4 pass, 1 fail (finding 1) |\n| `doctor` | 49 pass, 11 fail |\n\nThe 11 `doctor` failures are identical on `origin/release/v1.3.0` (49 pass, 11 fail), so they come from the host and not from this PR. There is no other `p10_*` test file and no `doctor*` file beyond `doctor.test.ts`. I did not run `doctor_providers` or `doctor_state_scan`.\n\n**Not checked**\n\n- Rust parity test.\n- Real `--resume` through the CLI process.\n- The `isNewObjective` and steering path, which could start a fresh counter by design.\n- Whether the compaction and findings calls are admitted elsewhere.\n- Managed-policy interaction, beyond grep.\n- The `eval_*` tests.\n\nBoth worktrees are removed.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>65961</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>15</tool_uses><duration_ms>303626</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
