{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"3fb0f3db2a696278b5f6c454a41511a83232fb0d669916d01d8e8ee61d719379","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015JCpXqAxZJs9Xoh28JFHqs","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev760.md","content":"**Independent review at `75a838be1a3d73c4eeda0224a65d86d0c9f63735` — REQUEST CHANGES (one blocker, a stale fixture; the budget logic itself held up)**\n\nCI at this head is red on `test-shard (22, 1)`, `(22, 2)`, `(24, 1)` and `(24, 2)`; the run was still in progress when this was written, so I have not read those logs. One failure reproduces locally:\n\n**Blocking**\n\n1. `cli/test/protocol_parity.test.ts` fails at this head (\"checked-in schema samples equal a fresh generation\") and passes 5/5 on `release/v1.3.0`. `sidecar-v1.schema.json` changed, but `cli/test/fixtures/protocol_v1_schema_samples.jsonl` was not regenerated: the full `history` sample lacks `inferenceSubmissions`, `maxInferenceSubmissions` and `inferenceSubmissionHistoryComplete`. Run `node cli/scripts/gen_protocol_samples.mjs` and commit the fixture; the Rust parity test reads the same file.\n\n**Not blocking: say what the bound covers**\n\n2. The bound is on the primary turn loop only (`run_turn.ts`, the `beforeSubmit` hook). The docs say subagents and durable operation units are not counted. Three side calls that also send a model request are uncounted and unmentioned: findings extraction (`agent.ts:3307`), the compaction probe (`agent.ts:3758`) and the compaction summary (`agent.ts:3797`). List them, or count them. WP-P10-02's title is \"aggregate budgets across direct, delegated, retry and resume paths\"; delegated paths are still outside it, which the progress note should state as remaining work.\n3. A project `.env` can set `NEXUS_MAX_INFERENCE_SUBMISSIONS` (it is in `PROJECT_ENV_KEYS`, `config.ts:188`), so a repository can raise a new objective's ceiling from 1,000 to 10,000. This follows `NEXUS_MAX_TOOL_INVOCATIONS`; the docs should say a project can set it. A raise on resume is blocked (`Math.min(saved, configured)`).\n4. Without durable state the counter is per turn (`ExecutionTracker.fresh()`, `run_turn.ts:160`); the docs do not say so.\n\n**Held up**\n\n- At the limit the turn ends `LIMIT_REACHED` / `INFERENCE_SUBMISSION_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED`, outcome `NOT_ESTABLISHED`; nothing retries afterwards; a limit of N allows exactly N submissions.\n- The reservation is saved before dispatch, and a failed save sends no request. A malformed counter or ceiling throws before any inference. Invalid configuration throws (minimum 1, default 1,000, maximum 10,000).\n- Retries, resume of a durable objective, continuation segments and alternate-provider selection are all counted.\n- Protocol changes are additive: new ledger entries only, `schema_version` stays 1.\n- Mutations: disabling the admission check, not counting retries, and resetting the counter on resume each fail the new test file.\n\n**Tests at this head:** `p10_inference_submission_budget` 4/4, `run_json_contract` 15, `protocol_schema` 8, `context_convergence` 57, `protocol_parity` 4 pass and 1 fail. `doctor.test.ts` fails 11 here and the same 11 on the release branch (host state).\n\n**Not checked:** the Rust parity test, a real `--resume` through the CLI, the new-objective and steering path, managed-policy interaction beyond reading.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FEDQYhf3cMhLJWhtfTR27S","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && gh pr comment 760 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev760.md | tail -1; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) REVIEW (claude-invariants-audit): #760 (P10-02 inference submission budget) at 75a838be REQUEST CHANGES, posted: protocol_parity fails (schema samples fixture not regenerated; run cli/scripts/gen_protocol_samples.mjs); CI red on four shard legs. Budget logic held up under mutation; docs should name the uncounted side calls and that a project .env can set the ceiling. #759 merged (24992b1f). #758 still REQUEST CHANGES.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Post the review on PR 760 and log it"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
