{"parentUuid":"9491c88e-a25d-4425-adac-ddaec44095d8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLf7rxpUBMNcfHVQgnrh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both open PRs got new commits (#758 and #760), so I'm sending each for a re-review against its earlier findings."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":556,"cache_read_input_tokens":489284,"output_tokens":3812,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":100},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":556,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3812,"cache_read_input_tokens":489284,"cache_creation_input_tokens":556,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":556},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChLf7rmuMEfTvuPj39cgc","requestRef":"2c2ae1a7-7bb2-42d7-8b41-122430b42fa0","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"46231741-6ca2-4d32-b929-d9891ecb3b1d","timestamp":"2026-11-23T22:35:32.454Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"46231741-6ca2-4d32-b929-d9891ecb3b1d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLf7rxpUBMNcfHVQgnrh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SJWxsm12VWueZxCaTv3gW7","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Re-review PR #758 new head","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Re-review GitHub PR #758 in the repo at ~/nexus-code (`gh pr view 758 --comments`, `gh pr diff 758`), \"fix(goal): pause stale boot goals with visible reason (PA-3 …)\", base `release/v1.3.0`. The previous review (the long comment on the PR beginning \"Independent review at `8d5b5465…`\") requested changes. The author pushed a new head (short `725a4435`; take the full SHA from `gh pr view 758 --json headRefOid`, review exactly that, and check at the end whether it moved). Look at `git diff 7320b78a..<new> -- cli docs` for what changed.\n\nVerify, by running:\n1. BLOCKER 1: a process restart (not only a host reboot) must leave a previously active goal PAUSED with a visible reason. Previously the \"boot id\" was `/proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id`, so a crash or clean exit followed by a restart on the same boot left the goal RUNNING; a state with no `activeBootId` (written before the PR) also stayed RUNNING; on hosts without `/proc` nothing paused. Check the new mechanism: what identifies \"this process\", how liveness of the previous owner is decided (pid reuse? a lock? a nonce?), and that these cases come back PAUSED: state RUNNING / WAITING / BLOCKED written by another (dead) process identity; state with no identity field at all; and that a goal owned by a process that is STILL ALIVE (a second concurrent `nexus` on the same state) is not wrongly paused or stolen. Already PAUSED / COMPLETE / CANCELLED goals must be left as they were. Drive the real functions with seeded state files in a throwaway HOME (see how `cli/test/goal_lifecycle.test.ts` builds state), not only by reading.\n2. BLOCKER 2: the test must exercise it. Remove the stale-owner checks (wherever they now live) and confirm `cli/test/goal_lifecycle.test.ts` fails; restore with `git checkout`. Confirm the tests seed non-paused states with a foreign identity and with none, and no longer return early / pass vacuously on hosts without `/proc`.\n3. Earlier non-blocking items, status only: `pauseReason ?? stale` hiding the stale reason behind an older operator reason; the doc `docs/v1.3.0/PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md` stating exactly what is covered; `delete (state as any)…` casts.\n4. The delta must not let model text, a tool call or workspace content change a goal's lifecycle state, and must not loosen approval, budget or managed-policy checks (`cli/src/core/policy_runtime.ts`); does resuming a paused goal go through the same checks as starting one?\n5. The token-usage commit `7320b78a` (rolled-up sub-operation token usage in `cli/src/goal.ts`, `goal_command.ts`): any way it misreports, double counts, or exposes data it should not? Light check.\n6. Run at head, one file at a time: every `cli/test/goal*.test.ts` and `cli/test/operation*.test.ts`; for any failure check the same file on `origin/release/v1.3.0`.\n\nMandatory rules:\n- Do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/rev758b <full sha>`; `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/rev758b/cli/`; copy `~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui}` into `~/nexus-wt/rev758b/core/target/release/`. Remove the worktree at the end (`git -C ~/nexus-code worktree remove --force ~/nexus-wt/rev758b`). No commits, pushes or GitHub comments.\n- Every run uses a throwaway HOME: `cd cli && HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20`, foreground, one file at a time, timeout at most 9 minutes (the runner prints `ℹ pass` / `ℹ fail`). Probe scripts live in a separate scratch directory. Never read the real ~/.nexus, /etc/nexus or ~/.config/nexus. No live inference, no network.\n- Stop every process you start by its own pid; never `pkill -f`. No background loops. Aim for about 30 minutes.\n- Shell is zsh (use `bash -c` for loops); output passes through `rtk` (use `rtk proxy <cmd>` if it looks filtered).\n\nReport under 450 words: verdict (ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS / REQUEST CHANGES) at the exact full SHA; each blocker fixed / partly / not with file:line and what you ran; status of the non-blocking items; new findings ranked, blocking vs not; mutation result; test counts; what you did not check."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":556,"cache_read_input_tokens":489284,"output_tokens":3812,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":100},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":556,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3812,"cache_read_input_tokens":489284,"cache_creation_input_tokens":556,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":556},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":15573,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01SJWxsm12VWueZxCaTv3gW7":{"description":"Re-review PR #758 new head","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Re-review GitHub PR #758 in the repo at ~/nexus-code (`gh pr view 758 --comments`, `gh pr diff 758`), \"fix(goal): pause stale boot goals with visible reason (PA-3 …)\", base `release/v1.3.0`. The previous review (the long comment on the PR beginning \"Independent review at `8d5b5465…`\") requested changes. The author pushed a new head (short `725a4435`; take the full SHA from `gh pr view 758 --json headRefOid`, review exactly that, and check at the end whether