{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"01c070ee04e23d69bdbe48ad01c1337362920246caf44dd83d1c63d808c4fa14","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WHMDE1HH9zrrWjywHqV2VU","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev758b.md","content":"**Re-review at `725a4435260fac0e90cfe631a861f7146420c6c2` — REQUEST CHANGES (the goal fix works; the same change breaks an existing test on the shared operation path)**\n\n**Blocker 1, restart detection: mostly fixed.** The owner is now `activePid` plus `activeHost` (`cli/src/goal.ts:65-79`, set at `goal.ts:280`), with liveness from `process.kill(pid, 0)`. Run against seeded state through the real `goalStatus`: RUNNING, WAITING and BLOCKED with a dead pid, with a foreign boot id, and with no identity at all each come back PAUSED with a reason; PAUSED, CANCELLED and COMPLETE are left alone; a goal whose owner is alive stays RUNNING, so a second concurrent `nexus` is neither paused nor stolen.\n\n**Blocker 2, the test: fixed for goals.** With `staleDriverReason` forced to return undefined, `goal_lifecycle.test.ts` goes from 7 passing to 5 pass, 2 fail.\n\n**New, blocking: a regression in `driveOperation`.**\n\n`cli/test/operation_entry_integrity.test.ts` (\"a stale snapshot … not written back over COMPLETE\") fails at this head (2 pass, 1 fail: PAUSED instead of COMPLETE) and passes 3 of 3 on `release/v1.3.0`.\n\nCause: `operation.ts:570` plans operations as RUNNING with no identity, and `driveOperation` now treats any existing RUNNING operation without identity as stale (`operation_runner.ts`, about lines 735-745). A freshly planned operation resumed through `operation_cli.ts:391`, `loop.ts:471` or `batch.ts:223` can therefore be paused before it has ever run.\n\nFix options: apply the \"no identity means stale\" rule in goal code only; or stamp the identity when planning; or skip the rule for an operation that has never run. Then add a `driveOperation` test for the stale path (no test references `pauseForStaleDriver` today).\n\n**Not blocking**\n\n- Limits the doc should list: a reused pid reads as alive, so that goal is never paused; a state from another host, or with a pid and no host, stays RUNNING; a state with only the current boot id and no pid stays RUNNING.\n- `pauseReason ?? stale` still hides the restart reason behind an older operator reason (probed: only the operator text is reported).\n- The host-boot test still returns early without `/proc` (`goal_lifecycle.test.ts:187`).\n- The reason text needs an edit: \"left active by earlier process (pid N) is no longer running\", \"left active by an earlier process left it active…\".\n- The `(state as any)` casts have multiplied (`operation_runner.ts:784-792`).\n- Token usage (`7320b78a`): reads totals and counts only, exposes no content, no double counting between reported and estimated; `agentRuns` may include retries.\n\n**Tests at this head, run one file at a time:** `goal_lifecycle` 7/0, `goal_ledger_propagation` 2/0, and thirteen `operation*` files, all passing except `operation_entry_integrity` (2 pass, 1 fail).\n\n**Not checked:** Node 22, a host without `/proc`, two live processes racing, an approval or budget check on the resume path.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WNrzL75yEcFBCxo167mc5N","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && gh pr comment 758 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev758b.md | tail -1; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) REVIEW (claude-invariants-audit): #758 re-review at 725a4435 REQUEST CHANGES, posted: goal restart detection now works (pid+host), but operation_entry_integrity.test.ts fails at head and passes on release: driveOperation pauses any RUNNING operation without identity, including a freshly planned one. Not mergeable.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"; gh run list --branch release/v1.3.0 --workflow ci.yml --limit 1 --json status,conclusion,headSha --jq '.[0]|[.status,.conclusion,.headSha[0:8]]|@tsv'; gh pr checks 758 2>&1 | rtk proxy grep -E \"^test-matrix|^test-.*fail\" | cut -c1-45","description":"Post the re-review on PR 758, log it, and read the release CI and 758's checks"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
