{"parentUuid":"6a76899a-39ed-4088-8162-8ce7cea31f0c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLiK3QXAq4EHfyshq1UH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0167xrxstiZDgH1fnM5RMbHV","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Review PR #761 flight log integrity","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Independent pre-merge review of GitHub PR #761 in the repo at ~/nexus-code (`gh pr view 761`, `gh pr diff 761`), \"fix(audit): expose skipped flight log records\", base `release/v1.3.0`, branch `v1/p10-03-flight-log-integrity`. Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 761 --json headRefOid`, review exactly that, and check at the end whether it moved. Files: `cli/src/flight.ts`, `cli/test/hash_chain.test.ts`, `docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` (+75/−11).\n\nContext: the flight recorder writes a hash-chained log of a session (GV-3: `cli/src/core/hash_chain.ts`, `cli/src/flight.ts`, verified by `nexus replay` / the audit bundle code `cli/src/core/audit*` from GV-2). The PR says: when payload redaction or an append fails, mark recording as degraded, return an explicit `recordingSkipped` event without stopping the authorised tool action, and disable subsequent chaining \"so the existing flight verifier reports broken or unchained evidence instead of accepting a later chain that omitted a record\".\n\nAnswer with file:line evidence, running things where practical:\n1. The core claim: after a record is skipped, can the remaining log still VERIFY as an intact chain (i.e. can a session with an omitted record pass `nexus replay` integrity / audit verify as if complete)? Construct it: use the recorder API as `cli/test/hash_chain.test.ts` does, force a redaction failure and an append failure (mock fs / a read-only file / an unserialisable payload), then run the real verifier over the resulting file. Also the reverse: does a healthy session still verify, and does degraded state persist across a recorder restart on the same file (a new process appending to a file whose last record was skipped — does it resume chaining from the last good hash and thereby hide the gap)?\n2. Can a model, tool output or workspace content TRIGGER a skip on purpose (e.g. a payload that makes redaction throw, an oversized or cyclic argument, invalid UTF-16) and thereby turn off the audit trail for the rest of the session while tool actions continue? The PR chooses to continue the tool action when recording fails: is that choice visible to the operator (a warning on stderr/TUI, a field in the turn result or receipt, the audit bundle marking the session degraded), or silent? Is there, or should there be, a managed-policy/strict option to stop instead? State plainly whether \"an attacker-controlled input can disable recording and keep acting\" holds, and how detectable it is afterwards.\n3. Does the `recordingSkipped` event itself get recorded anywhere durable, with what content (must not contain the unredacted payload that failed redaction)? Any path where the raw payload is logged in an error message?\n4. Verification outcomes: does anything downstream (receipts, `nexus verify`, audit export/verify) treat a degraded/unchained flight log as acceptable evidence?\n5. Tests: do the new tests fail if the degraded marking is removed, and if chaining continues after a skip? Mutate (then `git checkout`) and run `cli/test/hash_chain.test.ts`. Run at head, one file at a time: `hash_chain`, `audit_command`, `audit_bundle`, `audit_export` (whichever exist), any `flight*`/`replay*` test files, `trace_transparency`. For a failure, check the same file on `origin/release/v1.3.0`.\n6. The plan-doc change: does it claim only what code and tests show?\n\nMandatory rules:\n- Do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/rev761 <full sha>`; `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/rev761/cli/`; copy `~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui}` into `~/nexus-wt/rev761/core/target/release/`. Remove the worktree at the end (`git -C ~/nexus-code worktree remove --force ~/nexus-wt/rev761`). No commits, pushes or GitHub comments.\n- Every run uses a throwaway HOME: `cd cli && HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20`, foreground, one file at a time, timeout at most 9 minutes (the runner prints `ℹ pass` / `ℹ fail`). Probe scripts live in a separate scratch directory. Never read the real ~/.nexus, /etc/nexus or ~/.config/nexus. No live inference, no network.\n- Stop every process you start by its own pid; never `pkill -f`. No background loops. Aim for about 30 minutes.\n- Shell is zsh (use `bash -c` for loops); output passes through `rtk` (use `rtk proxy <cmd>` if it looks filtered).\n\nReport under 500 words: verdict (ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS / REQUEST CHANGES) at the exact full SHA; findings ranked with file:line, each marked confirmed-by-running or by-reading, blocking vs non-blocking; mutation results; test counts; what you did not check."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":661,"cache_read_input_tokens":511497,"output_tokens":1951,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":661,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1951,"cache_read_input_tokens":511497,"cache_creation_input_tokens":661,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":661},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":17409,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0167xrxstiZDgH1fnM5RMbHV":{"descript