{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:21:48.716Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a7ff865090af4d524</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_0167xrxstiZDgH1fnM5RMbHV</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/a7ff865090af4d524.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Review PR #761 flight log integrity\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>**Verdict: ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS** at `d24997ea926da335ff0e91ba8e88aca810831651`. The head did not move during the review. The worktree is removed. I made no commits, pushes or comments, and I ran no processes in the background.\n\n**Findings, ranked**\n\n1. **Non-blocking, confirmed by running: the gap is hidden if the recorder restarts before another write.**\n   - Sequence: `session_start`, `c1`, then `c2` is skipped (cyclic argument), the process stops, and a new `FlightRecorder` on the same id appends `c3` and `session_end`.\n   - `resumeChain` (`flight.ts:~88-92`) finds the file intact and resumes from the last good hash.\n   - `loadFlight` then reports `chain intact (4 records), closed by its session end`, with `c2` absent.\n   - The `chained=false` flag lives only in memory, and the skip leaves nothing on disk.\n   - Restart on a skipped log does stay broken if a later record was already written (probe D).\n   - Fix: on a skip, write a durable chained marker record if the disk allows. If it does not, accept that a trailing skip is undetectable and say so in the plan doc.\n\n2. **Non-blocking, confirmed by running, then by reading: the skip is invisible to the operator.**\n   - Every caller discards the return value (`dispatch_tool_call.ts:235` and the `recordToolResult` calls).\n   - `recordingSkipped` appears only in `flight.ts:136` and `161`. There is no stderr or TUI warning, no turn-result or receipt field, and no counter.\n   - The tool action continues, and the only trace is an unchained log read later.\n   - Fix: add a recorder `degraded` getter and a one-time stderr warning. Consider a strict managed-policy option to stop. The plan doc defers this, and it is not implemented.\n\n3. **Non-blocking, confirmed by running: attacker-controlled input can disable chaining for the rest of the session.**\n   - A cyclic argument gave `sanitization_failed` (probe A) and a BigInt gave `sanitization_failed` (probe B).\n   - Most of the cyclic and BigInt effect comes from the redactor throwing, not from the append.\n   - Recording continues, but unchained. Detection afterwards is real: the log reads `CHAIN BROKEN at position 2`.\n   - \"An attacker-controlled input can make recording degrade while actions continue\" holds. The skipped record is never seen, and the later ones are unprotected.\n   - Whether a model can supply a cyclic or BigInt value depends on how tool arguments are parsed. JSON-parsed model arguments cannot be cyclic. I did not trace that.\n\n4. **Non-blocking, by reading: a broken flight log does not fail audit verify.**\n   - A log that was already broken at export time produces a note, not a finding (`audit_bundle.ts:1014`). `audit_export.ts:676` warns on export.\n   - That is existing GV-2 behaviour, but the PR's \"verifier reports broken\" claim relies on it.\n\n5. **Nit, confirmed by running: a skip on the first record (probe F) reads as `not chained (... written before hash chaining)`.** That wording is misleading. Consider a distinct message.\n\n**Your numbered questions**\n\n- **Q1:** a healthy session verifies as `chain intact (3 records), closed`. A mid-session skip followed by a write reads `CHAIN BROKEN` (probes A, B, D). A trailing skip with no later write reads as intact and not closed (probe E). Restart after a trailing skip reads as intact and closed (finding 1).\n- **Q3:** the skip event is never written to disk. The payload holds only `{recordingSkipped, reason}`. Both `catch` blocks are bare, so the raw payload cannot appear in an error message. This is good.\n- **Q4:** I found no downstream use of `recordingSkipped`. Nothing treats a degraded log as explicitly acceptable. Finding 4 applies.\n- **Q6:** the plan doc matches the code and tests. The line \"reads as CHAIN BROKEN\" is true only when a later record is written, which is finding 1. The 4-line PR #760 progress text is unrelated churn.\n\n**Mutations of `cli/test/hash_chain.test.ts`** (each reverted with `git checkout`)\n\n| Mutation | Pass | Fail |\n|---|---|---|\n| Baseline | 27 | 0 |\n| All `chained = false` lines removed | 25 | 2 (both new tests) |\n| Only the two skip sites removed | 25 | 2 (both new tests) |\n\nThe new tests do catch the chaining continuing after a skip. No test covers a restart after a skip, and none checks operator visibility.\n\n**Other test files at head**\n\n| File | Pass | Fail |\n|---|---|---|\n| `audit_command` | 6 | 0 |\n| `audit_bundle` | 24 | 0 |\n| `audit_export` | 18 | 0 |\n| `flight_exclude` | 8 | 0 |\n| `flight_sanitization` | 3 | 0 |\n| `trace_transparency` | 14 | 0 |\n\nNo `replay*` test file exists.\n\n**Not checked**\n- The `nexus replay` CLI end to end. I used `FlightPlayer.loadFlight` and `describeIntegrity`, the same verifier code.\n- Whether model-supplied arguments can actually reach the recorder as a cyclic or BigInt value.\n- The behaviour of `audit verify` on a bundle with a broken flight log, which I confirmed only by reading.\n- Node 22.\n\nProbe script: `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/p/probe.mts`</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>49539</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>15</tool_uses><duration_ms>244725</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
