{"parentUuid":"fda4908b-8a57-4202-acc8-38e35d245c3b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLiet1XRP4FxSZeX6GpZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PBFffyn84f69w8ervsKFX3","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev761.md","content":"**Independent review at `d24997ea926da335ff0e91ba8e88aca810831651` — ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS**\n\nThe change does what it says in the main case and is an improvement on the branch: a healthy session reads `chain intact`, and a skip followed by any later write reads `CHAIN BROKEN`. Removing the `chained = false` lines fails both new tests (25 pass, 2 fail). The skip event carries only `{recordingSkipped, reason}`, and both `catch` blocks are bare, so the payload that failed redaction cannot reach a message.\n\n**Follow-ups, in order of weight**\n\n1. **A restart hides a trailing skip** (confirmed by running). Sequence: `session_start`, `c1`, `c2` skipped (cyclic argument), the process stops, a new `FlightRecorder` on the same id appends `c3` and `session_end`. `resumeChain` (`flight.ts`, about lines 88-92) finds the file intact and resumes from the last good hash; the log then reads `chain intact (4 records), closed by its session end` with `c2` absent. The degraded state is in memory only and the skip leaves nothing on disk. If a later record had been written before the restart, the log stays broken. Either write a durable chained marker on a skip when the disk allows, or state in the plan document that a skip which is the last event before a restart cannot be detected. The plan's line \"reads as CHAIN BROKEN\" is true only when a later record is written.\n2. **The operator is not told.** Every caller discards the return value (`dispatch_tool_call.ts:235` and the `recordToolResult` calls); `recordingSkipped` appears only at `flight.ts:136` and `161`. No warning, no field in the turn result or receipt, no counter. The action continues and the only trace is an unchained log read later. A `degraded` getter with a one-time warning would do; a strict managed-policy option to stop instead is worth considering.\n3. **An input can degrade recording for the rest of the session** (confirmed by running with a cyclic argument and with a BigInt: both give `sanitization_failed`). Later records are written unchained. Whether a model can supply such a value was not traced: arguments parsed from JSON cannot be cyclic or BigInt.\n4. **A broken flight log does not fail `audit verify`**: a log already broken at export time produces a note, not a finding (`audit_bundle.ts:1014`; `audit_export.ts:676` warns on export). Existing GV-2 behaviour, by reading, but \"the verifier reports broken\" leans on it.\n5. A skip on the first record reads as `not chained (... written before hash chaining)`, which misdescribes it.\n\nNo test covers a restart after a skip or operator visibility.\n\n**Tests at this head, 0 failures:** `hash_chain` 27, `audit_command` 6, `audit_bundle` 24, `audit_export` 18, `flight_exclude` 8, `flight_sanitization` 3, `trace_transparency` 14.\n\n**Not checked:** `nexus replay` end to end (the same verifier code was driven through `FlightPlayer.loadFlight`), `audit verify` on a bundle with a broken log by running, Node 22.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2642,"cache_read_input_tokens":514476,"output_tokens":1949,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":69},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2642,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1949,"cache_read_input_tokens":514476,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2642,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_inpu