{"parentUuid":"3e8f1b80-ac0a-49ed-b9f1-59d523520703","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLkciR1LiFrnG5yG2Y6p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01379tUbWz1vk5p5dGnUQMTv","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && gh pr comment 762 --body \"**Review at \\`e989ef6b\\` (the author's \\`26ecfda6\\` plus a merge of \\`release/v1.3.0\\`; I read the source change myself: 20 lines in \\`run_turn.ts\\`, one test) — ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS, pending green required checks.**\n\nWhat it does holds up by reading and by running the test on the merged branch (\\`turn_deadline_abort\\` 1/1; \\`p10_inference_submission_budget\\` 4/4, since #760 touched the same file; \\`tsc\\` clean):\n\n- The timer is armed once per turn and cleared on both exits of the function (after the loop, and in the \\`catch\\`). There is no \\`return\\` at function level between arming and clearing, so a stale timer cannot fire into a later turn.\n- Expiry goes through \\`requestCancel\\`, so it aborts the same signal an operator cancel does. \\`requestCancel\\` returns false when a cancel is already in progress, so an operator interrupt keeps its own reason, and the flag that turns the interruption into \\`TIME_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED\\` is set only when the deadline did the cancelling.\n- The result is a non-success budget outcome, not COMPLETED.\n\nFollow-ups, not blocking:\n\n1. **Guard the timer with \\`Number.isFinite(turnDeadline)\\`.** The timer is armed whenever \\`budget\\` is set, but the line above allows a non-finite \\`maxTurnMinutes\\` (deadline \\`Infinity\\`). \\`setTimeout\\` with an infinite or over-2³¹ ms delay fires after about 1 ms (confirmed in Node 24), which would cancel the turn at once as time-exhausted. Not reachable today: the budget is validated to at most 4,320 minutes and must be finite (\\`types.ts:208\\`). It is one condition away from a turn that dies on start.\n2. The test covers a deadline that expires during a streaming request. Nothing covers expiry during a tool call, or that a turn which ends normally leaves no timer behind (the leak guard would catch a pending timer only if the file imports it).\n3. As the PR says, cumulative elapsed time across turns and resumes, and per-tool deadlines, remain open.\" | tail -1; bash -c 'sleep 30; for i in $(seq 1 17); do c=$(gh pr checks 762 2>&1 | grep -E \"^(test-matrix|linux-x86_64)\" | grep -c pass); f=$(gh pr checks 762 2>&1 | grep -E \"^test-|^linux\" | grep -c fail); [ \"$c\" = 3 ] && break; [ \"$f\" != 0 ] && break; sleep 30; done; gh pr checks 762 2>&1 | grep -E \"^test-matrix|^linux-x86_64|^test-.*(fail|pending)\" | cut -c1-55; gh pr view 762 --json headRefOid,state --jq \"[.state,.headRefOid]|@tsv\"'","description":"Post the review on PR 762 and wait for its checks","timeout":590000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1407,"cache_read_input_tokens":531007,"output_tokens":1340,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":210},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1407,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1340,"cache_read_input_tokens":531007,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1407,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1407},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":9773,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01379tUbWz1vk5p5dGnUQMTv":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && gh pr comment 762 --body \"**Review at \\`e989ef6b\\` (the author's \\`26ecfda6\\` plus a merge of \\`release/v1.3.0\\`; I read the source change myself: 20 lines in \\`run_turn.ts\\`, one test) — ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS, pending green required checks.**\n\nWhat it does holds up by reading and by running the test on the merged branch (\\`turn_deadline_abort\\` 1/1; \\`p10_inference_submission_budget\\` 4/4, since #760 touched the same file; \\`tsc\\` clean):\n\n- The timer is armed once per turn and cleared on both exits of the function (after the loop, and in the \\`catch\\`). There is no \\`return\\` at function level between arming and clearing, so a stale timer cannot fire into a later turn.\n- Expiry goes through \\`requestCancel\\`, so it aborts the same signal an operator cancel does. \\`requestCancel\\` returns false when a cancel is already in progress, so an operator interrupt keeps its own reason, and the flag that turns the interruption into \\`TIME_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED\\` is set only when the deadline did the cancelling.\n- The result is a non-success budget outcome, not COMPLETED.\n\nFollow-ups, not blocking:\n\n1. **Guard the timer with \\`Number.isFinite(turnDeadline)\\`.** The timer is armed whenever \\`budget\\` is set, but the line above allows a non-finite \\`maxTurnMinutes\\` (deadline \\`Infinity\\`). \\`setTimeout\\` with an infinite or over-2³¹ ms delay fires after about 1 ms (confirmed in Node 24), which would cancel the turn at once as time-exhausted. Not reachable today: the budget is validated to at most 4,320 minutes and must be finite (\\`types.ts:208\\`). It is one condition away from a turn that dies on start.\n2. The test covers a deadline that expires during a streaming request. Nothing covers expiry during a tool call, or that a turn which ends normally leaves no timer behind (the leak guard would catch a pending timer only if the file imports it).\n3. As the PR says, cumulative elapsed time across turns and resumes, and per-tool deadlines, remain open.\" | tail -1; bash -c 'sleep 30; for i in $(seq 1 17); do c=$(gh pr checks 762 2>&1 | grep -E \"^(test-matrix|linux-x86_64)\" | grep -c pass); f=$(gh pr checks 762 2>&1 | grep -E \"^test-|^linux\" | grep -c fail); [ \"$c\" = 3 ] && break; [ \"$f\" != 0 ] && break; sleep 30; done; gh pr checks 762 2>&1 | grep -E \"^test-matrix|^linux-x86_64|^test-.*(fail|pending)\" | cut -c1-55; gh pr view 762 --json headRefOid,state --jq \"[.state,.headRefOid]|@tsv\"'","description":"Post the review on PR 762 and wait for its checks","timeout":590000}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChLkciEay7SzYv12NS5v8","requestRef":"155d9251-709b-4317-bab3-bfcf454b4d8a","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"fd9dcbc8-2f0c-4c12-99d8-e19e426fcd31","timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:47:48.522Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
