{"parentUuid":"9ccee2c7-2008-4c84-bdb3-65ecbed570e1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLsy9jt1ejMz7HGP9ajn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GBZZDseemGhaQ5u74D75ny","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Review PR #763 flight gaps","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Independent pre-merge review of GitHub PR #763 in the repo at ~/nexus-code (`gh pr view 763`, `gh pr diff 763`), \"fix(audit): preserve flight recording gaps\", base `release/v1.3.0`. Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 763 --json headRefOid`, review exactly that, and check at the end whether it moved. Files: `cli/src/audit_contract.ts`, `cli/src/core/audit_bundle.ts`, `cli/src/flight.ts`, tests `cli/test/{audit_bundle,audit_command,audit_export,audit_schema,hash_chain}.test.ts`, `docs/AUDIT.md`, `docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`, files under `docs/protocol`.\n\nContext: this follows PR #761 (merged), which made the flight recorder (hash-chained session log, `cli/src/flight.ts`, `cli/src/core/hash_chain.ts`) mark recording degraded and stop chaining when redaction or an append fails. The review of #761 (read it: `gh pr view 761 --comments`, the comment beginning \"Independent review at `d24997ea…`\") left these follow-ups, which this PR presumably addresses:\n 1. A restart hid a trailing skip: `session_start, c1, [c2 skipped], process stops, new FlightRecorder on the same id appends c3, session_end` read as \"chain intact (4 records), closed\", because the degraded state was only in memory and `resumeChain` resumed from the last good hash.\n 2. The operator was not told (every caller discarded the `recordingSkipped` return; no warning, no field, no counter).\n 3. An input that makes redaction throw (a cyclic value, a BigInt) degraded recording for the rest of the session.\n 4. `audit verify` treated a flight log that was already broken at export time as a note, not a finding (`audit_bundle.ts` ~1014, `audit_export.ts` ~676).\n 5. A skip on the first record read as \"not chained (… written before hash chaining)\".\n\nVerify by running wherever practical (drive the real `FlightRecorder` / `FlightPlayer.loadFlight` / `describeIntegrity` and the audit export + verify code in a throwaway HOME, the way the existing tests and the earlier probe did):\nA. Follow-up 1: reproduce the exact restart sequence above and variants (skip is the very last event then restart; skip then crash with no restart; two skips; skip on the first record; skip caused by an append failure such as a read-only file or ENOSPC-like error rather than redaction). In each, what does the verifier report, and can ANY sequence with an omitted record still read as an intact, closed chain? If a durable gap marker is now written: is the marker itself chained/tamper-evident, what happens when the marker cannot be written either (disk failure is the very case that causes a skip), and can a marker be forged or removed by someone who can edit the log without the verifier noticing?\nB. Follow-up 4: does `nexus audit export` / `audit verify` now fail or flag (which: exit status, finding, note?) for a bundle whose flight log has a recorded gap or a broken chain? Does a healthy bundle still verify? Is the bundle/contract schema change additive and versioned per the repo's rules (frozen older schema versions untouched; version ledgers under `docs/protocol` updated; `cli/test/audit_schema.test.ts`)? Would an older verifier reading a new bundle, or the new verifier reading an older bundle, misreport?\nC. Follow-ups 2, 3, 5: status of each. Is the gap marker's content free of the payload that failed redaction?\nD. Nothing here weakens an existing finding or lets a tampered bundle verify: check the tamper tests still fail closed (one changed byte fails and names the file).\nE. Mutations (then `git checkout`): remove the durable-gap write; make audit verify ignore a gap; run `hash_chain`, `audit_bundle`, `audit_command`, `audit_export` test files — do they fail?\nF. Run at head, one file at a time: `hash_chain`, `audit_bundle`, `audit_command`, `audit_export`, `audit_schema`, `flight_exclude`, `flight_sanitization`, `trace_transparency`, `leak_guard`, `protocol_parity`, `protocol_schema`. For any failure, check the same file on `origin/release/v1.3.0`.\nG. Docs (`docs/AUDIT.md`, the plan): claim only what code and tests show?\n\nMandatory rules:\n- Do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/rev763 <full sha>`; `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/rev763/cli/`; copy `~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui}` into `~/nexus-wt/rev763/core/target/release/`. Remove the worktree at the end (`git -C ~/nexus-code worktree remove --force ~/nexus-wt/rev763`). No commits, pushes or GitHub comments.\n- Every run uses a throwaway HOME: `cd cli && HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20`, foreground, one file at a time, timeout at most 9 minutes (the runner prints `ℹ pass` / `ℹ fail`). Probe scripts live in a separate scratch directory (an earlier probe you may read and adapt, by copying, is at `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/p/probe.mts`). Never read the real ~/.nexus, /etc/nexus or ~/.config/nexus. No live inference, no network.\n- Stop every process you start by its own pid; never `pkill -f`. No background loops. Aim for about 35 minutes.\n- Shell is zsh (use `bash -c` for loops); output passes through `rtk` (use `rtk proxy <cmd>` if it looks filtered).\n\nReport under 550 words: verdict (ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS / REQUEST CHANGES) at the exact full SHA; for each of the five follow-ups: fixed / partly / not, with file:line and what you ran; new findings ranked, blocking vs non-blocking; mutation results; test counts; what you did not check."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1141,"cache_read_input_tokens":559544,"output_tokens":2371,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1141,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2371,"cache_read_input_tokens":559544,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1141,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1141},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":21556,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01GBZZDseemGhaQ5u74D75ny":{"description":"Review PR #763 flight gaps","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Independent pre-merge review of GitHub PR #763 in the repo at ~/nexus-code (`gh pr view 763`, `gh pr diff 763`), \"fix(audit): preserve flight recording gaps\", base `release/v1.3.0`. Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 763 --json headRefOid`, review exactly that, and check at the end whether it moved. Files: `cli/src/audit_contract.ts`, `cli/src/core/audit_bundle.ts`, `cli/src/flight.ts`, tests `cli/test/{audit_bundle,audit_command,audit_export,audit_schema,hash_chain}.test.ts`, `docs/AUDIT.md`, `docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`, files under `docs/protocol`.\n\nContext: this follows PR #761 (merged), which made the flight recorder (hash-chained session log, `cli/src/flight.ts`, `cli/src/core/hash_chain.ts`) mark recording degraded and stop chaining when redaction or an append fails. The review of #761 (read it: `gh pr view 761 --comments`, the comment beginning \"Independent review at `d24997ea…`\") left these follow-ups, which this PR presumably addresses:\n 1. A restart hid a trailing skip: `session_start, c1