ds the skip.\n\n**Blocker**\n- `cli/test/flight_sanitization.test.ts:157` fails at head and passes on `origin/release/v1.3.0` (3/3). Its \"classifier failure skips flight and audit persistence\" test asserts that no flightlog file exists. The new marker write creates one, so `AutonomousAgent` now leaves a durable log after a sanitizer failure. Either update the test and state this as intended, or skip the marker when no log exists yet. Merging as is breaks CI.\n\n**Non-blocking**\n- Make the gap durable even when the marker write fails, for example a sidecar or an in-record flag, or fail closed on resume when the last write failed. Without that, follow-up 1 does not hold for ENOSPC.\n- Make `audit verify` treat `unchained` plus a `recording_gap` record as a finding. This would also need the manifest to carry the skip.\n- The new finding kind extends an enum in the v1 schema. The ledger gains a new `schemaSha256` entry with `schema_version` still 1. This follows the earlier GV-2 additive precedent. A consumer that validates strictly against the old enum would reject the new kind. The bundle format itself is unchanged.\n- The new verifier now returns `tampered` for old bundles whose exported log was already broken, where it used to return `intact_unsigned`. That is intended, but `docs/AUDIT.md` should say it changes verdicts on existing bundles.\n- Marker content is fixed: `{recordingSkipped:true, reason}` only. No failed payload appears, and the test checks this for the classifier text.\n\n**Mutations** (each reverted)\n- Removing the marker write fails 2 tests in `hash_chain`. The audit files pass, so no audit test needs the marker.\n- Making verify ignore a broken-at-export log fails 1 test each in `audit_bundle`, `audit_command` and `audit_export`.\n\n**Tests at head** (fail counts: only `flight_sanitization` has any)\n\n| File | Pass |\n|---|---|\n| `hash_chain` | 28 |\n| `audit_bundle` | 24 |\n| `audit_command` | 7 |\n| `audit_export` | 18 |\n| `audit_schema` | 