{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"e3c031fbcb39323737f8ca8df94a4b9a529c532ce0ed02b9567edf733d323197","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NvC1T1nQysP8ePd2tC2Q9r","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev763.md","content":"**Independent review at `748863d201a75f953121ff4703576c8481ae82aa` — REQUEST CHANGES (one test regression; the rest is progress on the #761 follow-ups)**\n\n**Blocking**\n\n- `cli/test/flight_sanitization.test.ts:157` fails at this head (2 of 3) and passes on `release/v1.3.0` (3 of 3). \"classifier failure skips flight and audit persistence\" asserts that no flight log file exists; the new marker write creates one, so a sanitizer failure now leaves a durable log behind. Either that is intended, and the test and its name change to say what is left on disk, or the marker is not written when no log exists yet.\n\n**The #761 follow-ups, each run**\n\n1. **A restart hiding a trailing skip: fixed when the marker can be written.** The exact sequence (`session_start`, `c1`, skip, restart, `c3`, `session_end`) now reads \"recording skipped…\", chain broken at position 3. A trailing skip with no restart, and two skips, are flagged too.\n   **Still open: when the marker cannot be written either.** With the append made to fail (a directory where the log file belongs), then restored and restarted, the log reads \"chain intact (4 records), closed\" with `recordingSkipped: false`. A disk failure is the case that causes a skip, so this is the same hole in the case that matters most. Options: a second place for the flag, or failing closed on resume when the last write failed. If it stays, `docs/AUDIT.md` and the plan must state it; their wording about keeping degraded status across a restart is true only when the marker was written.\n2. **Operator not told: fixed.** `process.emitWarning`, once per recorder, code `NEXUS_FLIGHT_RECORDING_DEGRADED`, also when a recorder resumes a degraded log.\n3. **One failed redaction ends chaining for the session: unchanged.** Now visible, still permanent.\n4. **`audit verify` on a log broken at export: fixed for chained logs.** New finding `log_not_intact_at_export`; a mid-log skip and a restart after a skip both give exit 1 `tampered`; a healthy bundle exit 0. Removing it fails one test each in `audit_bundle`, `audit_command` and `audit_export`.\n   **Gap:** a skip on the first record leaves a log with no chained record, so the bundle is `unchained` and verify returns exit 0 `intact_unsigned` with only the \"not chained when exported\" note. The bundle carries nothing about the skip.\n5. **First-record skip wording: fixed in `describeIntegrity` and replay**, not in `audit verify` (see 4).\n\n**Not blocking**\n\n- The marker is unchained by design. A forged marker on a healthy log reads as skipped and broken, which fails closed. Deleting the marker and every later record leaves a clean prefix that verifies; that is the documented limit of the chain, and the marker adds no tamper evidence of its own.\n- The new finding kind extends an enum in the v1 audit schema, with a new `schemaSha256` ledger entry and `schema_version` still 1 (the earlier additive precedent). A consumer validating strictly against the old enum rejects the new kind.\n- The new verifier returns `tampered` for existing bundles whose exported log was already broken, where it used to return `intact_unsigned`. Intended; `docs/AUDIT.md` should say verdicts on existing bundles can change.\n- The marker holds `{recordingSkipped: true, reason}` only; the test checks the classifier text is absent.\n\n**Tests at this head:** `hash_chain` 28, `audit_bundle` 24, `audit_command` 7, `audit_export` 18, `audit_schema` 7, `flight_exclude` 8, `trace_transparency` 14, `leak_guard` 6, `protocol_parity` 5, `protocol_schema` 8, all passing; `flight_sanitization` 2 of 3.\n\n**Not checked:** a byte-flip probe separate from the existing tamper tests (which pass), an older verifier on a new bundle, a signed bundle, Node 22.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B4BJQRq45x4VfWA4TKtqkk","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && gh pr comment 763 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev763.md | tail -1; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) REVIEW (claude-invariants-audit): #763 (flight recording gaps) at 748863d2 REQUEST CHANGES, posted: flight_sanitization.test.ts:157 fails at head, passes on release (the gap marker creates a log file after a sanitizer failure). Still open by design question: when the marker cannot be written (disk failure), a restart again reads as intact. Release tip d03e6199 green; real-server LSP suite passes there.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"; gh pr checks 763 2>&1 | rtk proxy grep -E \"^test-matrix|^linux|^test-.*fail\" | cut -c1-45; gh pr view 763 --json headRefOid --jq '.headRefOid[0:8]'","description":"Post the review on PR 763, log it, and read its checks"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
