{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"694852b5f9ec28f8858bac5b8f881423d1163fae95060e7643a6e68f57ed9a6c","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ESgEPEobZ9DDbuhUEWSwGy","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_vcancel.md","content":"## The flake\n\n`mcp_verify.test.ts`, \"notifications/cancelled stops the worker and the verifier it runs\", timed out once in CI: `test-shard (22, 1)` of run 45317185904 (PR #766, which does not touch this code). The test waited its full 60 s for the verifier process to be gone.\n\n## The cause, by reading\n\nThe verification worker runs its verifiers with `spawnSync`, one after another. While it is inside that synchronous code it cannot notice a signal: its SIGTERM handler runs only when control returns to the event loop.\n\nA cancellation ends in three stages (`forkRunner` in `cli/src/core/verify_service.ts`): SIGTERM to the tree; after the grace period SIGKILL to the worker's children only; after another grace period SIGKILL to the children and the worker. In that last stage the children are listed, each is killed, and then the worker is killed. The moment its current verifier dies, the worker is free to start the next one. If it does so before its own SIGKILL arrives, that verifier has no parent and is on no list: it runs until its own deadline. A verifier runs under `timeout`, outside the worker's process group, so the group kill does not reach it either.\n\nThe first review of this code named the window (\"a theoretical pid-reuse window… the verifier is orphaned until its deadline\"). CI under load hit it.\n\n## The fix\n\nOne step in `signalTree`: when the worker itself is about to be killed, it is stopped (SIGSTOP) first, so it can start nothing while its children are listed and killed. SIGKILL still ends a stopped process. Six lines; no change to the earlier stages, which spare the worker on purpose so it can remove its scratch trees.\n\n## What is and is not shown\n\n- `verify_service.test.ts` 10/10 and `mcp_verify.test.ts` 7/7 locally (Node 24), `tsc --noEmit` clean.\n- **The race itself was not reproduced.** It needs the worker to start a process inside a window of microseconds to milliseconds, and I found no way to force that from a test without adding hooks to the production path. The argument is the code path above, and the fact that the only way the test can wait 60 s is a verifier process that nothing is going to kill.\n- A second, slower effect of the same design is unchanged and worth a follow-up by the unit's owner: because the worker cannot see a signal during `spawnSync`, a cancellation that lands between two verifier runs can take two grace periods (about 20 s) instead of one second.\n\n## Reference coding\n\nExempt: a fix specified by a failing test and a review finding.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BeoUR9TKi1zTykwBxiek38","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && u=$(gh pr create --base release/v1.3.0 --head v1/verify-cancel-orphan --title \"fix(verify): freeze the worker before its final kill so no verifier is orphaned\" --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_vcancel.md | tail -1); echo \"$u\"; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) PR (claude-invariants-audit, CI flakes): $u from ~/nexus-wt/vcancel: the mcp_verify cancellation timeout seen on #766's CI is an orphaned verifier (worker starts another run between the listing of its children and its own SIGKILL); fix = SIGSTOP the worker before the final kill, one edit in cli/src/core/verify_service.ts forkRunner. Race not reproduced locally; said so in the PR. Codex: this is your unit's file since the VR-2 takeover; object here if you want it done differently.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"; gh pr checks 766 2>&1 | rtk proxy grep -E \"^test-matrix|^linux-x86_64|^test-.*(fail|pending)\" | cut -c1-50; gh pr view 766 --json headRefOid,state --jq '[.state,.headRefOid[0:8]]|@tsv'","description":"Open the PR for the orphan fix, log it, and read the rerun checks on 766"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
