{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-24T03:50:28.536Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>aaa81cc7d6cb7775f</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01BsHdNsPjqBcez5nvi5PUxD</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/aaa81cc7d6cb7775f.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Review PR #767 orphan fix\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>**Verdict: ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS at 8ab2e902b320ca462a58b721364ed7b87abfd607.** The PR head did not move, but #767 is already merged (merge commit 2dea2179). I tested \"base\" as 061843fc, the first parent of that merge.\n\n**1. Diagnosis: partly holds.**\n- Each verification runs several verifiers back to back. `execute` in `verify.ts:1110-1130` and `executorIn` in `verify.ts:1280` both call `checkpoint()` before running.\n- `checkpoint()` (`verify.ts:738-741`) awaits `setImmediate`, which turns the event loop and lets the SIGTERM handler (`verify_worker.ts:14`) run. So a worker that was sent SIGTERM aborts at the next gap between verifiers.\n- That makes the race narrower than the PR text says. The worker has to get past `checkpoint()` and into `spawnSync` after its verifier was killed but before its own SIGKILL. That is plausible only under load.\n- The race is not reproduced, and the PR says so itself. The freeze is harmless, and it shrinks the window.\n- Uncovered window, reproduced: `signalTree` (`verify_service.ts:172-185`) takes one `ps` snapshot and then kills. A descendant that forks after the snapshot, such as `timeout` starting `bwrap`, survives. The stage-3 kill hits `timeout` but misses the new `bwrap`, which is then orphaned.\n- Stages 1 and 2 are covered by the next stage, as long as the worker is still alive to trigger it.\n- If the worker exits on its own after stage 2, `finish` clears the timer. Stage 3 never runs, and descendants of a dead worker can no longer be found through `ps`.\n- `onProcessExit` (line 195) runs `signalTree(\"SIGKILL\")` synchronously, which is fine. The `ps` call inside it takes up to 5 s.\n\n**2. Correctness (by reading).**\n- `child.pid` undefined returns early. A dead pid makes `kill` throw, and that is caught.\n- Pid reuse between the SIGSTOP and the SIGKILL is microseconds wide and no worse than before.\n- A stopped worker is always followed by a SIGKILL in the same call. The group kill at line 183 also covers it. The only way it stays stopped is if SIGKILL throws. That is unlikely, and `kill` is already being called on a process the server owns.\n- The freeze only applies when `worker &amp;&amp; name === \"SIGKILL\"`. Stage 2 passes `worker=false`, so it is unchanged.\n- The `exit` and `disconnect` events fire normally after a SIGKILL of a stopped process.\n- Scratch trees: a SIGKILLed worker could not clean up before this change either. The service and tests do not remove them at that stage. The watchdog test at `verify_service.test.ts:288` only covers the spared path.\n- Windows: not checked. SIGSTOP does nothing there, and `try/catch` hides the failure.\n\n**3. Loop results.** My script is `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/loop.mts`. It aborts the verifier at a random 0-400 ms with `killGraceMs` 150, then looks for a marker process 300 ms later.\n\n| | Plain `sleep` | `trap '' TERM; sleep` |\n|---|---|---|\n| Head | 30 runs, 0 orphans | about 140 runs, 2 orphans |\n| Base (061843fc) | 30 runs, 0 orphans | 110 runs, 0 orphans |\n\n- Both head orphans were `bwrap` with ppid 1, with cancellation roughly 200 ms after start. That is the post-snapshot fork window above.\n- Two of 140 against zero of 110 is not a significant difference. I do not read it as a regression from the freeze.\n- Part of the head TRAP count came from two copies of that run that I started by mistake and that ran at the same time.\n- I did not reproduce the original worker race at either commit.\n\n**4. Tests at head.**\n- `verify_service`: 10 of 10 pass.\n- `mcp_verify`: 7 of 7 pass.\n- `leak_guard`: 6 of 6 pass.\n\n**Follow-up, not blocking.** Repeat `descendants()` and kill until no new descendants appear, or SIGSTOP each pid as it is found. Do it at least in the final stage.\n\n**Not checked.** macOS and Windows, Node 22, and the CI load conditions.\n\nThe worktrees are removed and no marker `sleep` is left running.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>57091</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>23</tool_uses><duration_ms>802900</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
