0/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/loop.mts`. It aborts the verifier at a random 0-400 ms with `killGraceMs` 150, then looks for a marker process 300 ms later.\n\n| | Plain `sleep` | `trap '' TERM; sleep` |\n|---|---|---|\n| Head | 30 runs, 0 orphans | about 140 runs, 2 orphans |\n| Base (061843fc) | 30 runs, 0 orphans | 110 runs, 0 orphans |\n\n- Both head orphans were `bwrap` with ppid 1, with cancellation roughly 200 ms after start. That is the post-snapshot fork window above.\n- Two of 140 against zero of 110 is not a significant difference. I do not read it as a regression from the freeze.\n- Part of the head TRAP count came from two copies of that run that I started by mistake and that ran at the same time.\n- I did not reproduce the original worker race at either commit.\n\n**4. Tests at head.**\n- `verify_service`: 10 of 10 pass.\n- `mcp_verify`: 7 of 7 pass.\n- `leak_guard`: 6 of 6 pass.\n\n**Follow-up, not blocking.** Repeat `descendants()` and kill until no new descendants appear, or SIGSTOP each pid as it is found. Do it at least in the final stage.\n\n**Not checked.** macOS and Windows, Node 22, and the CI load conditions.\n\nThe worktrees are removed and no marker `sleep` is left running.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>57091</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>23</tool_uses><duration_ms>802900</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}]}}
