{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","id":"22c6144a-9df0-4248-9750-770e8a2018bd","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:41:20.879Z","version":"2.1.329","querySource":"repl_main_thread","shapeHash":"a54769307b2b572ea56dcd7775d3ef4272884106ee45fff28a82ca7c150a39c1","params":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"819e90b6-2f91-4106-acec-ab0cdee46c94","keep":1052,"tail":["20d87b50d0f216567d590eaa55f41e32322654784625668f31697fc19d9af6d2","46b55f80d5a646eb8c9982a03d6cf11abab6973d447c3f69a78981b99b4f3e31","3bad71dc3ffc775ae082591b64158248819f867b7d394ad69feea31c98514778"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",1054,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"afa7f5e2441ba5395ef995642c26cb7635e6d18331264fef9e0474d51bd56f89"}
{"type":"file-history-delta","messageId":"25b241cf-ebf5-4d98-9647-f5bdf151acb6","snapshotMessageId":"abca5e7e-c323-4cf5-8f4e-c8b6a618b236","trackingPath":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_vkill.md","backup":{"backupFileName":null,"version":1,"backupTime":"2026-11-24T04:41:35.766Z","realParentDir":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad"},"timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:41:35.772Z"}
{"type":"data-flow-records","v":1,"sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","records":[{"response_id":"msg_011ChM91wWFbnCa2soKGoBTa","mark_sent_by":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","listed":["msg_011ChM8iAAFnk2DcbgDTCzbR"]}]}
{"parentUuid":"479a081d-c29e-4475-af75-84401e34f502","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChM91wWFbnCa2soKGoBTa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019qhaTpL4ney8Z7vpMqa21k","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_vkill.md","content":"Follow-up to #767, whose review found that my diagnosis there was only partly right and that a different window is the one that can be reproduced.\n\n## What actually leaves a verifier behind\n\nCancelling a verification signals the worker's process tree in stages (`forkRunner` → `signalTree` in `cli/src/core/verify_service.ts`). Each stage took one process listing and signalled what was on it. Two things escape that:\n\n1. **A fork after the listing.** `timeout` starts the sandbox, and the sandbox starts its inner process. A process forked after the listing is on no list.\n2. **A parent that dies of the signal.** When the outer sandbox process dies of SIGTERM and the inner one ignores it, the inner one is handed to init. No later listing finds it under the worker, so the later stages never touch it, and if the worker then exits, those stages do not run at all.\n\nThe result is a sandbox process with parent 1 that runs until the verifier's own deadline. That is what `mcp_verify.test.ts` waited 60 s for in CI.\n\n## The fix\n\n- **Every stage stops the tree before it signals it**: the worker and its descendants get SIGSTOP from the top down, one listing at a time, until a listing adds nothing. A stopped process starts nothing, so each further listing can only add what was started before its parent stopped. Then the signal is sent, and everything that is not being killed gets SIGCONT.\n- **Every process seen is remembered with its kernel start time.** A remembered process that is still running (same pid, same start time) is treated as a root in later listings and is signalled even when it is no longer below the worker. The start time is what keeps a reused pid from being hit.\n- **When a cancelled worker exits, survivors are swept** with a final kill, because the timed stages are cancelled at that point.\n\n`descendants()` now takes several roots. The earlier stages still spare the worker so it can remove its scratch trees.\n\n## Measured\n\nA cancel loop from the review of #767 (real `VerifyService`, a verifier that ignores SIGTERM, cancellation at a random 0–400 ms, kill grace 150 ms, then a search for any process carrying the run's marker):\n\n| Version | Runs | Orphans |\n|---|---|---|\n| `release/v1.3.0` with #767 | about 140 | 2 |\n| freeze the worker, repeat the listing in the kill stages only | 120 | 1 |\n| plus remembered processes and the sweep | 320 | 3 |\n| this PR (stop the tree in every stage) | 340 | 0 |\n\nWith a plain `sleep` verifier: 40 runs, 0 orphans. All earlier orphans were the sandbox process with parent 1, at a cancellation about 150–200 ms after start. At the earlier rate (roughly 1 in 70), 340 clean runs would be expected about once in a hundred tries, so this is strong evidence and not proof.\n\n`verify_service.test.ts` 10/10, `mcp_verify.test.ts` 7/7, `tsc --noEmit` clean (Node 24).\n\n## Limits\n\n- The start time comes from `/proc`. Where there is no `/proc`, a process is not remembered, and the behaviour is the listing-with-stop alone.\n- A process that leaves the tree before it is ever listed (double-forks within the first milliseconds) is still unseen. The sandbox does not do this.\n- Not tested: Node 22 locally, the Docker sandbox engine.\n- No deterministic test for the race was added: it needs a cancellation inside a window of a few milliseconds. The loop above is how it was measured; the script is not part of the repository.\n\n## Reference coding\n\nExempt: a fix specified by a failing test and a review finding.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":736,"cache_read_input_tokens":641666,"output_tokens":2378,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":736,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2378,"cache_read_input_tokens":641666,"cache_creation_input_tokens":736,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":736},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":13597,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_019qhaTpL4ney8Z7vpMqa21k":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_vkill.md","content":"Follow-up to #767, whose review found that my diagnosis there was only partly right and that a different window is the one that can be reproduced.\n\n## What actually leaves a verifier behind\n\nCancelling a verification signals the worker's process tree in stages (`forkRunner` → `signalTree` in `cli/src/core/verify_service.ts`). Each stage took one process listing and signalled what was on it. Two things escape that:\n\n1. **A fork after the listing.** `timeout` starts the sandbox, and the sandbox starts its inner process. A process forked after the listing is on no list.\n2. **A parent that dies of the signal.** When the outer sandbox process dies of SIGTERM and the inner one ignores it, the inner one is handed to init. No later listing finds it under the worker, so the later stages never touch it, and if the worker then exits, those stages do not run at all.\n\nThe result is a sandbox process with parent 1 that runs until the verifier's own deadline. That is what `mcp_verify.test.ts` waited 60 s for in CI.\n\n## The fix\n\n- **Every stage stops the tree before it signals it**: the worker and its descendants get SIGSTOP from the top down, one listing at a time, until a listing adds nothing. A stopped process starts nothing, so each further listing can only add what was started before its parent stopped. Then the signal is sent, and everything that is not being killed gets SIGCONT.\n- **Every process seen is remembered with its kernel start time.** A remembered process that is still running (same pid, same start time) is treated as a root in later listings and is signalled even when it is no longer below the worker. The start time is what keeps a reused pid from being hit.\n- **When a cancelled worker exits, survivors are swept** with a final kill, because the timed stages are cancelled at that point.\n\n`descendants()` now takes several roots. The earlier stages still spare the worker so it can remove its scratch trees.\n\n## Measured\n\nA cancel loop from the review of #767 (real `VerifyService`, a verifier that ignores SIGTERM, cancellation at a random 0–400 ms, kill grace 150 ms, then a search for any process carrying the run's marker):\n\n| Version | Runs | Orphans |\n|---|---|---|\n| `release/v1.3.0` with #767 | about 140 | 2 |\n| freeze the worker, repeat the listing in the kill stages only | 120 | 1 |\n| plus remembered processes and the sweep | 320 | 3 |\n| this PR (stop the tree in every stage) | 340 | 0 |\n\nWith a plain `sleep` verifier: 40 runs, 0 orphans. All earlier orphans were the sandbox process with parent 1, at a cancellation about 150–200 ms after start. At the earlier rate (roughly 1 in 70), 340 clean runs would be expected about once in a hundred tries, so this is strong evidence and not proof.\n\n`verify_service.test.ts` 10/10, `mcp_verify.test.ts` 7/7, `tsc --noEmit` clean (Node 24).\n\n## Limits\n\n- The start time comes from `/proc`. Where there is no `/proc`, a process is not remembered, and the behaviour is the listing-with-stop alone.\n- A process that leaves the tree before it is ever listed (double-forks within the first milliseconds) is still unseen. The sandbox does not do this.\n- Not tested: Node 22 locally, the Docker sandbox engine.\n- No deterministic test for the race was added: it needs a cancellation inside a window of a few milliseconds. The loop above is how it was measured; the script is not part of the repository.\n\n## Reference coding\n\nExempt: a fix specified by a failing test and a review finding.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChM91wCQGWCMo6FHx25VQ","requestRef":"22c6144a-9df0-4248-9750-770e8a2018bd","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"25b241cf-ebf5-4d98-9647-f5bdf151acb6","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:41:35.381Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"25b241cf-ebf5-4d98-9647-f5bdf151acb6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c797335f-b3ec-48e3-80ea-405ba86f8371","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019qhaTpL4ney8Z7vpMqa21k","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_vkill.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"e33cf022-e883-410a-b04d-28a158cfe399","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:41:36.745Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_vkill.md","content":"Follow-up to #767, whose review found that my diagnosis there was only partly right and that a different window is the one that can be reproduced.\n\n## What actually leaves a verifier behind\n\nCancelling a verification signals the worker's process tree in stages (`forkRunner` → `signalTree` in `cli/src/core/verify_service.ts`). Each stage took one process listing and signalled what was on it. Two things escape that:\n\n1. **A fork after the listing.** `timeout` starts the sandbox, and the sandbox starts its inner process. A process forked after the listing is on no list.\n2. **A parent that dies of the signal.** When the outer sandbox process dies of SIGTERM and the inner one ignores it, the inner one is handed to init. No later listing finds it under the worker, so the later stages never touch it, and if the worker then exits, those stages do not run at all.\n\nThe result is a sandbox process with parent 1 that runs until the verifier's own deadline. That is what `mcp_verify.test.ts` waited 60 s for in CI.\n\n## The fix\n\n- **Every stage stops the tree before it signals it**: the worker and its descendants get SIGSTOP from the top down, one listing at a time, until a listing adds nothing. A stopped process starts nothing, so each further listing can only add what was started before its parent stopped. Then the signal is sent, and everything that is not being killed gets SIGCONT.\n- **Every process seen is remembered with its kernel start time.** A remembered process that is still running (same pid, same start time) is treated as a root in later listings and is signalled even when it is no longer below the worker. The start time is what keeps a reused pid from being hit.\n- **When a cancelled worker exits, survivors are swept** with a final kill, because the timed stages are cancelled at that point.\n\n`descendants()` now takes several roots. The earlier stages still spare the worker so it can remove its scratch trees.\n\n## Measured\n\nA cancel loop from the review of #767 (real `VerifyService`, a verifier that ignores SIGTERM, cancellation at a random 0–400 ms, kill grace 150 ms, then a search for any process carrying the run's marker):\n\n| Version | Runs | Orphans |\n|---|---|---|\n| `release/v1.3.0` with #767 | about 140 | 2 |\n| freeze the worker, repeat the listing in the kill stages only | 120 | 1 |\n| plus remembered processes and the sweep | 320 | 3 |\n| this PR (stop the tree in every stage) | 340 | 0 |\n\nWith a plain `sleep` verifier: 40 runs, 0 orphans. All earlier orphans were the sandbox process with parent 1, at a cancellation about 150–200 ms after start. At the earlier rate (roughly 1 in 70), 340 clean runs would be expected about once in a hundred tries, so this is strong evidence and not proof.\n\n`verify_service.test.ts` 10/10, `mcp_verify.test.ts` 7/7, `tsc --noEmit` clean (Node 24).\n\n## Limits\n\n- The start time comes from `/proc`. Where there is no `/proc`, a process is not remembered, and the behaviour is the listing-with-stop alone.\n- A process that leaves the tree before it is ever listed (double-forks within the first milliseconds) is still unseen. The sandbox does not do this.\n- Not tested: Node 22 locally, the Docker sandbox engine.\n- No deterministic test for the race was added: it needs a cancellation inside a window of a few milliseconds. The loop above is how it was measured; the script is not part of the repository.\n\n## Reference coding\n\nExempt: a fix specified by a failing test and a review finding.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"25b241cf-ebf5-4d98-9647-f5bdf151acb6","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"e33cf022-e883-410a-b04d-28a158cfe399","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChM91wWFbnCa2soKGoBTa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012BT2NEyo6E7aPiHrHMEx3n","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/vcancel && git fetch -q origin && git status --short && git commit -qam \"fix(verify): stop the process tree before signalling it, and remember what was seen\n\nA cancelled verification could leave a sandbox process running with no\nparent until the verifier's own deadline. Each signal stage took one process\nlisting: a process forked after the listing was on no list, and a sandbox\nwhose parent died of SIGTERM while it ignored the signal was handed to init,\nout of reach of every later stage.\n\nEvery stage now stops the tree from the top down until a listing adds\nnothing, signals it, and resumes what is not being killed. Every process seen\nis remembered with its kernel start time and signalled later even when it is\nno longer below the worker. A cancelled worker that exits has its survivors\nswept.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git merge -q origin/release/v1.3.0 --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -1; cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p . >/dev/null; echo \"tsc $?\"; cd .. && git push -q -u origin v1/verify-kill-until-empty 2>&1 | tail -1; echo \"remote: $(git ls-remote origin refs/heads/v1/verify-kill-until-empty | cut -c1-8) local: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"; cd ~/nexus-code && u=$(gh pr create --base release/v1.3.0 --head v1/verify-kill-until-empty --title \"fix(verify): stop the process tree before signalling it, and remember what was seen\" --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_vkill.md | tail -1); echo \"$u\"; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) PR (claude-invariants-audit, CI flakes): $u from ~/nexus-wt/vcancel. The review of #767 corrected my diagnosis and reproduced the real window (a sa