{"parentUuid":"fcbdbf58-6f40-43eb-a97f-ca6d0969fe5f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c797335f-b3ec-48e3-80ea-405ba86f8371","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jf55A732BpzpEpTSWEAieq","type":"tool_result","content":"-**Follow-up progress (2026-11-24, merged PR #761 review):** Sanitization and append failures now attempt to persist a payload-free, unchained `recording_gap` marker, retain degraded status across recorder restart, and emit one operator warning per recorder. If the filesystem also rejects the marker write, only the runtime warning survives; persistence cannot be guaranteed when the evidence sink is unavailable. `nexus replay` reports skipped evidence explicitly, including when the first record was skipped. Audit verification now returns a finding and nonzero result when a bundled log was already broken at export; an unchained legacy log remains a stated limitation. Regression tests cover restart after a trailing skip, warning content, first-record skip wording, and broken-at-export verification.\n+**Follow-up progress (2026-11-24, merged PR #763):** Sanitization and append failures now attempt to persist a payload-free, unchained `recording_gap` marker, retain degraded status across recorder restart, and emit one operator warning per recorder. If the filesystem also rejects the marker write, only the runtime warning survives; persistence cannot be guaranteed when the evidence sink is unavailable. `nexus replay` reports skipped evidence explicitly, including when the first record was skipped. Audit verification returns a finding and nonzero result when a bundled log was already broken at export; an unchained legacy log remains a stated limitation. The PR's required checks passed at head `a18ec4c991fa583b52ba6ead441e9afe7d5df36c`; post-merge CI passed on `c2faaa89922a21e90bb1916c654015d417b9b582` (run `45307469727`).\n+**Follow-up progress (2026-11-24, merged PR #764):** `nexus audit verify --json` now fails closed when the flight log contains a durable `recording_gap` marker, including when the marker is the first record and the remaining log is unchained. The verifier reports `tampered` with `log_recording_gap_at_export`; clean bundles retain their prior result. The limit when disk failure prevents the marker from being persisted is documented. Required checks passed at head `5e5bb11f72630c16cad54b71456b512e9a20f370`; post-merge CI passed on `b74edef04083fcdcb2a53b842790792a174e3bcc` (run `45309777194`).\n+**Progress (2026-11-24, merged PR #762):** `runTurnImpl` now arms a timer for the active turn's `maxTurnMinutes` deadline and requests cancellation while inference or a tool is still awaiting completion. Expiry returns `LIMIT_REACHED` / `TIME_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED`; the timer is cleared on normal completion and caught failure. Tests cover aborting slow streamed inference, stopping a running shell command before its later side effect, and clearing the timer after a normal turn. Exact-head CI passed o\n-**Progress (2026-11-24):** Measured the critical-path baseline at release commit `4d9996d485c2db866918c110d35e1c1a1d3b2911` using Babel's TypeScript parser. `runTurnImpl` is 1,262 lines / CC 324 / nesting 5; `dispatchToolCallImpl` is 900 / CC 288 / nesting 6; `runSubagent` is 209 / CC 70 / nesting 4; `compactNowImpl` is 63 / CC 17 / nesting 3; `driveOperation` is 47 / CC 17 / nesting 3. `make lint` now compares those named functions to that exact Git baseline, fails on any increase in CC or con\n+**Progress (2026-11-24, merged PR #766):** Measured the critical-path baseline at release commit `4d9996d485c2db866918c110d35e1c1a1d3b2911` using Babel's TypeScript parser. `runTurnImpl` is 1,262 lines / CC 324 / nesting 5; `dispatchToolCallImpl` is 900 / CC 288 / nesting 6; `runSubagent` is 209 / CC 70 / nesting 4; `compactNowImpl` is 63 / CC 17 / nesting 3; `driveOperation` is 47 / CC 17 / nesting 3. `make lint` now compares those named functions to that exact Git baseline, fails if a tracked\n-**Required tests / acceptance:** Existing exact-main CI evidence demonstrates the static gate passes on `9156571f7d5fd8f8436c3105f0237628ab35e857`; the same gate is required in the PR workflow. A changed critical function crossing an agreed, baseline-derived CC/nesting threshold fails a focused check. The verification policy remains exposed to single-user workflow changes until WP-P10-01 can be independently satisfied.\n+**Required tests / acceptance:** The focused tests prove that decision-count and nesting growth are rejected and that the tracked release-baseline functions pass. `make lint` runs in the required Node 22/24 and Linux CI gates. The gate also fails closed if a tracked function or baseline source cannot be resolved. The verification workflow remains changeable by the sole maintainer under the current single-user policy; independent protection is unavailable and must not be implied.\n-**Migration / rollback:** If historical warnings appear on a new toolchain, baseline them narrowly with tracked expiry/owner; do not suppress globally. Rollback is removal of a specific analyzer job only with independent approval. Residual risk: static analysis cannot establish requirements correctness or provider behavior.\n+**Migration / rollback:** If historical warnings appear on a new toolchain, baseline them narrowly with tracked expiry/owner; do not suppress globally. The sole maintainer may direct rollback of this specific gate; any rollback must be visible in the PR and must not be described as independently approved. Residual risk: static analysis cannot establish requirements correctness or provider behavior.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"dbc0bad0-8d44-43bc-8215-8adfc0da4582","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:44:00.008Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"-**Follow-up progress (2026-11-24, merged PR #761 review):** Sanitization and append failures now attempt to persist a payload-free, unchained `recording_gap` marker, retain degraded status across recorder restart, and em