{"type":"data-flow-records","v":1,"sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","records":[{"response_id":"msg_011ChMEx6FCLm7SdtYNBjtpi","mark_sent_by":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","listed":["msg_011ChMEvGBSoEiVcKwrwWhSz"]}]}
{"parentUuid":"a330e2be-f9cc-4d08-9a03-ee7a499ddd8b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMEx6FCLm7SdtYNBjtpi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The #771 review is back and posted on the PR as request changes. It should not merge as it stands, and I've put a do-not-merge note in the claims log for the other sessions.\n\n- **The blocker (confirmed by running):** `nexus audit export` would now run `git status` in whatever workspace the recorded state names, without disabling git filters. The reviewer built a repository with a clean filter configured and the filter's command ran. So an untrusted workspace could run a command in the shell of whoever runs an audit export. The underlying routine is shared and already has this exposure elsewhere; what's new is that the audit export, which should be safe to run on a workspace you don't trust, now calls it.\n- **Fix options:** disable filters the way `nexus verify` already does, or refuse a workspace that configures one, or report \"unavailable\" and document the exposure.\n- **Tests:** two test files failed at the reviewed head because their expectations were stale. The author's newest commit (`c615f6a1`) updates those expectations and changes no source, so the blocker applies to it unchanged.\n- **What held up:** hitting a size bound reports \"unavailable\", never \"matched\"; the new file is covered by the bundle's manifest hashes; it holds ids and statuses only.\n\nThe release branch is green at `5abbc4cb`, and #771 is the only open PR."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2158,"cache_read_input_tokens":677271,"output_tokens":430,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2158,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},