{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-24T06:17:36.979Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a0e852b5eac7d8129</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_011kta5PLogADoN1rmx6jLqT</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/a0e852b5eac7d8129.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Re-review PR #771 new head\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>**Verdict: REQUEST CHANGES at `64a3b05302bc465882c092f279702290877c2a14`.** The PR head has since moved to `3455d3f484cb82bf48e7f89dde041cec1c3b5cfb`, which I did not review. It is still open. I removed the worktree.\n\n**Blocker 1 is not fixed.** The delta from `7e58def9` to `64a3b053` touches only two test files (`audit_export.test.ts` and `audit_command.test.ts`). `candidate.ts` and `audit_export.ts` are unchanged. `docs/AUDIT.md` is untouched.\n\n**Hostile-repo probes.** Each repo got a tracked file whose mtime was bumped so git had to re-hash it. I drove both `computeCandidateIdentitySync` and the in-process `exportAuditBundle` with a seeded subject. I did not run the CLI entry. It calls the same function, so the result would be the same.\n\n| Vector | Function | Export |\n|---|---|---|\n| `filter.clean` | **executed** | **executed** |\n| `filter.process` | **executed** | **executed**; reported `unavailable` |\n| `core.fsmonitor=&lt;cmd&gt;` | **executed** | **executed** |\n| `include.path` pointing at a filter | **executed** | **executed** |\n| `includeIf` pointing at a filter | **executed** | **executed** |\n| `core.attributesFile` + filter | **executed** | **executed** |\n| `.git/info/attributes` + filter | **executed** | **executed** |\n| `.git` file pointing at a hostile gitdir with `core.worktree` | **executed** | **executed** |\n| `core.worktree` set + filter | **executed** | **executed** |\n| `filter.smudge`, `diff.x.textconv`, `core.sshCommand`, `core.pager`, `core.editor` | not executed | not executed |\n| `post-index-change`, `reference-transaction`, `pre-auto-gc` hooks | not executed | not executed |\n| alias on `status`, `.gitconfig` in the workspace | not executed | not executed |\n| bare repo in a subdirectory | not executed | not executed |\n\nThe claim that no configured program from the workspace runs is false. Nothing was refused as `unavailable` because of the exploit. The `.git`-file case passes `verifyCheckout` because `core.worktree` points back at the workspace.\n\nI did not confirm the submodule-with-filter vector. My fixture was a nested plain repo, not a registered submodule.\n\n`fsmonitor` runs even though `status` passes `-c core.fsmonitor=false`. Another git call (probably `ls-files -v`, `rev-parse` or `config`) does not carry that override.\n\nFix: pass `-c core.fsmonitor=false -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null` to every git call, plus `-c filter.*` overrides that fail closed, and set `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null`, `GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1`, `GIT_ATTR_NOSYSTEM=1`, `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT`, and so on. Or refuse any workspace whose config, includes or attributes mention a filter or fsmonitor and report `unavailable`.\n\n**Shared routine.** It is unchanged, so receipt digests are the same as before and existing receipts do not start mismatching. The flip side is that every candidate-identity caller shares the exposure: `agent.ts`, `spine_handlers.ts`, `worktree.ts`, `state.ts` and `operation_runner_execution.ts`. Only the audit export is new.\n\n**Legitimate cases** (same routine for receipt and export):\n\n| Repo | Before edit | After edit |\n|---|---|---|\n| plain | `matched` | `mismatch` |\n| `* text=auto` with a CRLF file | `matched` | `mismatch` |\n| real filter (`tr a-z A-Z`) | `matched` | `mismatch` |\n\nNo false `mismatch` appeared. A real filter runs during the export, which is the same bug.\n\n**New blocker: `audit_command` fails at this head** (7 pass, 1 fail). The commit \"expect missing receipt binding warning\" asserts `no_receipts` and a \"No persisted validation receipts\" warning. The fixture has a receipt, so the output is `candidate binding: partial` plus the \"could not be bound... or the report was truncated\" warning. The last delta commit broke this test.\n\n**Mutation testing.** I did not run it. There is no hardening to remove, and no test uses a hostile repo. `grep` finds no filter, untrusted-checkout or 50,000-entry / 256 MiB test. The earlier gap (item 7 of the first review) is open.\n\n**Earlier non-blocking items**\n- Item 3 (active worktree path vs recorded workspace path): not verified.\n- Item 4 (the `no_receipts` warning on every receipt-less export): still present, and the test now asserts it.\n- Item 5 (exit-status policy): not stated anywhere.\n- Item 6 (`docs/AUDIT.md`): not updated.\n\n**Test counts at `64a3b053`**\n\n| File | Pass | Fail |\n|---|---|---|\n| `audit_export` | 19 | 0 |\n| `audit_command` | 7 | 1 |\n| `audit_bundle` | 25 | 0 |\n| `audit_schema` | 7 | 0 |\n| `leak_guard` | 6 | 0 |\n| `verify_hostile` | 46 | 0 |\n| `verify_command` | 18 | 0 |\n\n`tsc --noEmit` is clean and `check_invariants` passes. I lost the `check_requirements` result because the run output was cut off. I did not compare the `audit_command` failure against `origin/release/v1.3.0`. It comes from the PR's own expectation edit.\n\n**Not checked:** the CLI entry end to end, a real registered submodule, the `core.worktree` and `.git`-file cases beyond the above, the new head `3455d3f4`, and the complexity gate.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>57189</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>24</tool_uses><duration_ms>908256</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
