{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","prNumber":771,"prUrl":"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/771","prRepository":"mikeholownych/nexus-code","timestamp":"2026-11-24T06:18:10.002Z"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"4b3c0f53e41e2f41500d203eb33dc9fec9a2a45f0be13821bcb2fb782f318933","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FAXEgNdmUwtMkJCp53K7Mz","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev771b.md","content":"**Re-review at `64a3b05302bc465882c092f279702290877c2a14` — REQUEST CHANGES. The head is now `3455d3f4`, which changes two lines of `audit_command.test.ts` and nothing else; everything about the source below applies to it.**\n\n**The blocker is not addressed.** Every commit since `7e58def9` touches test expectations only. `cli/src/core/candidate.ts` and `cli/src/audit_export.ts` are unchanged, and so is `docs/AUDIT.md`. Please do not merge this on green checks: the checks do not exercise a hostile workspace.\n\n**Programs configured in the workspace still run during `audit export`.** Each case below was run against both `computeCandidateIdentitySync` and the in-process `exportAuditBundle` with a seeded subject, on a throwaway repository whose tracked file had its mtime bumped so git had to re-hash it. \"Executed\" means the configured command wrote its marker file.\n\n| Vector | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `filter.<x>.clean` via `.gitattributes` | executed |\n| `filter.<x>.process` | executed (the export then reported `unavailable`) |\n| `core.fsmonitor=<command>` | executed |\n| `include.path` to a file that sets a filter | executed |\n| `includeIf` to a file that sets a filter | executed |\n| `core.attributesFile` naming the filter | executed |\n| `.git/info/attributes` naming the filter | executed |\n| `.git` as a file pointing at a gitdir elsewhere with `core.worktree` back at the workspace | executed (and `verifyCheckout` passes it) |\n| `core.worktree` set, with a filter | executed |\n| `filter.smudge`, `diff.textconv`, `core.sshCommand`, `core.pager`, `core.editor` | not executed |\n| `post-index-change`, `reference-transaction`, `pre-auto-gc` hooks | not executed |\n| an alias for `status`, a `.gitconfig` in the workspace, a bare repository in a subdirectory | not executed |\n\n`core.fsmonitor` runs although `git status` is given `-c core.fsmonitor=false`: another git call in the routine (`ls-files`, `rev-parse` or `config`) does not carry the override.\n\n**What a fix needs:** the same overrides on every git call the routine makes; filters and the fsmonitor disabled in a way that fails closed (command-line `-c` overrides, plus `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null`, `GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1`, `GIT_ATTR_NOSYSTEM=1`), or a refusal with `unavailable` for any workspace whose configuration, includes or attributes name a filter or an fsmonitor; and a test with at least the clean-filter case that fails when the hardening is removed. There is no hostile-repository test today.\n\nOne thing to settle while fixing: the routine is shared with `agent.ts`, `spine_handlers.ts`, `worktree.ts`, `state.ts` and `operation_runner_execution.ts`. Changing how it hashes would change receipt digests; changing only what it allows to execute would not. With today's code a legitimate repository behaves correctly (plain, `* text=auto` with a CRLF file, and a real filter each report `matched`, then `mismatch` after an edit), but the real filter runs during the export.\n\n**Tests at `64a3b053`:** `audit_command` 7 pass, 1 fail (the expectation added by \"expect missing receipt binding warning\" asserts `no_receipts`, while the fixture has a receipt and reports `partial`); `3455d3f4` appears to correct that. `audit_export` 19/0, `audit_bundle` 25/0, `audit_schema` 7/0, `leak_guard` 6/0, `verify_hostile` 46/0, `verify_command` 18/0, `tsc` clean, `check_invariants` passes.\n\n**Still open from the first review:** items 3 to 7 (worktree path versus recorded workspace path; the `no_receipts` warning on every receipt-less export, which a test now asserts; the exit-status policy; `docs/AUDIT.md`; no test for the two scan bounds or an untrusted checkout).\n\n**Not checked:** the CLI entry end to end (it calls the same function), a registered submodule with a filter, the head `3455d3f4` beyond its diff.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0132eQfpUfiMmKqw2GPodkaM","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && gh pr comment 771 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev771b.md | tail -1; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) REVIEW (claude-invariants-audit): #771 re-review at 64a3b053 REQUEST CHANGES, applies to 3455d3f4: the commits since the first review change test expectations only; candidate.ts and audit_export.ts are untouched. Nine git-configuration vectors execute a workspace-configured program during audit export (clean filter, process filter, core.fsmonitor, include.path, includeIf, core.attributesFile, .git/info/attributes, .git file to another gitdir, core.worktree). DO NOT MERGE #771 on green checks: no test exercises a hostile workspace. Also noted for whoever owns candidate.ts: the same exposure exists for every caller of the candidate-identity routine.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"; gh pr view 771 --json state,headRefOid --jq '[.state,.headRefOid[0:8]]|@tsv'; gh pr checks 771 2>&1 | rtk proxy grep -E \"^test-matrix|^linux-x86_64\" | cut -c1-40","description":"Post the re-review on PR 771, log a do-not-merge note, and re-read its state and checks"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
