{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-24T08:59:46.999Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ad7fea4d7926ff2ab</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01QkZCbELCFP3wBuXwKC1QbS</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/ad7fea4d7926ff2ab.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Probe audit export git check\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Source restored (guard line back to original), probe deleted, worktree removed. Here is the report.\n\n## Security probe: `workspace_configures_git_programs` guard in `audit_export.ts`\n\n**Tip SHA tested:** `4ae25a10d5e1f33726a717b0fe1970fbd5f06517` (`origin/release/v1.3.0`). git 2.43.0, Node ran via tsx. All 17+submodule cases ran once with the check, once with it disabled (`false &amp;&amp;`).\n\n### Results\n\n| Case | With check (exec? / binding / reason) | Check disabled (exec? / binding) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 01 clean filter (.git/config) | no / unavailable / workspace_configures_git_programs | **EXECUTED** / mismatch |\n| 02 filter.process | no / unavailable / …git_programs | **EXECUTED** / unavailable(candidate_identity_unavailable) |\n| 03 core.fsmonitor | no / unavailable / …git_programs | no / mismatch |\n| 04 include.path | no / unavailable / …git_programs | **EXECUTED** / mismatch |\n| 05 includeIf gitdir | no / **mismatch** / - | no / mismatch |\n| 06 core.attributesFile | no / unavailable / …git_programs | **EXECUTED** / mismatch |\n| 07 .git/info/attributes | no / unavailable / …git_programs | **EXECUTED** / mismatch |\n| 08 .git-file + core.worktree | no / unavailable / …git_programs | **EXECUTED** / mismatch |\n| 09 core.worktree | no / unavailable / …git_programs | **EXECUTED** / mismatch |\n| 10 extensions.worktreeConfig | no / unavailable / …git_programs | **EXECUTED** / mismatch |\n| 11 key-case fsMonitor | no / unavailable / …git_programs | no / mismatch |\n| 12 parser-desync subsection | no / unavailable / …git_programs | no / mismatch |\n| 13 hook post-index-change | no / **mismatch** / - | no / mismatch |\n| 14 submodule filter | **EXECUTED** / unavailable / candidate_identity_unavailable | **EXECUTED** / unavailable(candidate_identity_unavailable) |\n| 15 control A (none) | no / mismatch | no / mismatch |\n| 16 control B (operator global) | **EXECUTED** / mismatch | EXECUTED / mismatch |\n| 17 control C (lfs, no attrs) | no / unavailable / …git_programs | no / mismatch |\n\n### (a) Bypasses — planted program EXECUTED with the check enabled\n- **Case 14 (registered submodule).** A `filter.p.clean` planted in `.git/modules/sub/config` plus `sub/.gitattributes` **ran the marker command with the check enabled.** The guard only lists config of the top-level `workspacePath`; the submodule's own config is invisible to `git config --get-regexp` at the superproject root, so the guard returns \"no hit\", then `computeCandidateIdentitySync` hashes files inside `sub/` and fires the planted filter. The binding ends `unavailable / candidate_identity_unavailable` (the filter errored the scan) — so the refusal is incidental, not the guard catching it; the code already executed. This is a real bypass of the stated invariant (\"nothing planted in an untrusted workspace executes with the exporter's rights\").\n\n### (b) Cases that prove nothing (did not execute even with the check disabled)\n- 03 core.fsmonitor, 11 core.fsMonitor (case variant), 13 post-index-change hook, 05 includeIf gitdir, 12 parser-desync, 17 lfs-without-attrs. None run during candidate-identity hashing (fsmonitor/hooks aren't invoked by the hash path; the includeIf/desync/no-attrs variants never produced an active filter). They tell us only that the guard still *reports* unavailable for 03/11/12/17; they do not demonstrate an execution vector. 05 and 13 aren't even flagged (binding=mismatch), but also never execute, so no bypass.\n\n### (c) Controls — all behaved as expected\n- A (no config): not executed, mismatch. B (operator's `$HOME/.gitconfig` global filter): EXECUTED, mismatch — correctly *allowed*, scope `global` is trusted. C (lfs clean, no `.gitattributes`): unavailable/workspace_configures_git_programs — the documented over-refusal trade-off.\n\n### Not run / caveats\nEverything requested ran in one pass (no compile retries needed). The submodule bypass (14) is the actionable finding; I did not attempt to fix it or confirm whether a deeper `--get-regexp` scope walk or pre-scan refusal would close it.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>82845</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>16</tool_uses><duration_ms>330700</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
