{"parentUuid":"308853c8-ab8c-47b7-8969-26d018a4844a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMVh5KE1CMwAyMo91REq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The submodule fix is up as #776. I'm sending it for a short independent review before it merges, then turning to the first build tracks as they report."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2113,"cache_read_input_tokens":784807,"output_tokens":1954,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":38},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2113,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1954,"cache_read_input_tokens":784807,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2113,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2113},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChMVh4doMMAC4JbZ1S666","requestRef":"c7a5eefc-aa7a-4a87-8775-5392e0c36752","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"d37c22d6-5e8d-4870-a4fb-9d5c4769a324","timestamp":"2026-11-24T09:12:30.064Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"d37c22d6-5e8d-4870-a4fb-9d5c4769a324","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMVh5KE1CMwAyMo91REq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FucdE1HVy6uCDG67HjSqap","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Review PR #776 submodule check","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Short, time-boxed independent review (aim for 20 minutes) of GitHub PR #776 in the repo at ~/nexus-code (`gh pr view 776`, `gh pr diff 776`), \"fix(audit): do not hash a workspace that has a submodule\", base `release/v1.3.0`. Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 776 --json headRefOid`, review exactly that, and check at the end whether it moved or was merged. The change is in `repositoryConfiguresPrograms` in `cli/src/audit_export.ts` (about 15 lines) plus one new test at the end of `cli/test/audit_export.test.ts` (\"a workspace with a submodule is not hashed…\").\n\nContext in three sentences: `nexus audit export` computes a candidate identity for the workspace named by recorded state, which runs `git status` there; a check refuses (binding `unavailable`, reason `workspace_configures_git_programs`) a repository whose own git configuration names a program git would run, so that nothing planted in an untrusted workspace executes. A probe found that a registered submodule's own configuration (`.git/modules/<name>/config`) is not seen by that check and its clean filter ran. This PR additionally refuses a workspace whose index holds a gitlink (mode 160000 in `git ls-files --stage`) or whose git directory has anything under `modules/`, and removes an early `return false` that skipped everything after the config listing.\n\nCheck, by running where it is quick:\n1. Run `cli/test/audit_export.test.ts` at head (throwaway HOME). Then disable the two submodule conditions (copy the source file aside first and restore from the copy; do not use `git checkout` to undo) and confirm the new test fails with \"the submodule's configured command ran\".\n2. Ways a submodule-like nested repository can still be read by `git status` without tripping the new conditions. Try these three in throwaway repos, driving the real export as the new test does (read the test and reuse its helpers by writing your probe as an extra untracked test file `cli/test/zz_probe776.test.ts` that you delete afterwards; print results instead of asserting): (a) a nested plain git repository in a subdirectory that is NOT registered as a submodule (no gitlink in the index, nothing under `.git/modules`) with a filter in its own `.git/config` and a tracked-in-the-inner-repo file re-stamped (same content and size, new mtime via `fs.utimesSync`) — does the outer `git status --untracked-files=all` descend into it and run the inner filter? (b) a gitlink added to the index with `git update-index --add --cacheinfo 160000,<sha>,sub` pointing at a nested repo — refused by the new condition? (c) a submodule that is registered and then has its gitlink removed from the index (`git rm --cached sub`) while `.git/modules/sub` remains — refused by the `modules/` condition? Fixture rule: after planting the filter configuration, run no git command yourself in that workspace (your own command would run the planted program); the planted command is `sh -c 'echo ran > <marker>; cat'` with the value double-quoted in the config file.\n3. Read the function once more for: any path that returns \"no\" (false) on an error; whether `git ls-files --stage` or `git rev-parse --absolute-git-dir` could themselves run a planted program (they should not: say so or show otherwise); the 256 MiB `maxBuffer` (a huge index → `status` null → counted as a hit?).\n4. False refusals: a plain repository with no submodule still compares (`mismatch` with the fake receipt id the test uses); say so from the existing tests.\n\nRules: do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/rev776 <full sha>`; `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/rev776/cli/`; `mkdir -p ~/nexus-wt/rev776/core/target/release && cp ~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui} ~/nexus-wt/rev776/core/target/release/`. Tests: `cd ~/nexus-wt/rev776/cli && HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20`, foreground. Never read the real ~/.nexus, /etc/nexus, ~/.config/nexus or ~/.gitconfig. No network. Stop any process by its own pid; never `pkill -f`. No commits, pushes or GitHub comments. At the end delete your probe file and run `git -C ~/nexus-code worktree remove --force ~/nexus-wt/rev776`. Shell is zsh (use `bash -c` for loops); output passes through `rtk` (prefix `rtk proxy` if it looks filtered). If you run out of time, report what you have.\n\nReport under 350 words: verdict (ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS / REQUEST CHANGES) at the exact SHA; results of 1; a three-row table for 2 (executed? binding status and reason); findings from 3 with file:line; what you did not check."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2113,"cache_read_input_tokens":784807,"output_tokens":1954,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":38},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2113,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1954,"cache_read_input_tokens":784807,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2113,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2113},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":17315,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01FucdE1HVy6uCDG67HjSqap":{"description":"Review PR #776 submodule check","subagent_type":"re