{"parentUuid":"c4921935-07a7-4e75-a362-67d0329f8848","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMWZSWpKtNpY4n7C4fmr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HhzQA4RwkngLHdFCWgxbFb","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Review PRs #774 and #775","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Independent pre-merge review of TWO GitHub PRs in the repo at ~/nexus-code, both based on `release/v1.3.0` and written by another agent. Time-box: about 40 minutes total; give each a verdict even if partial, and say what you did not reach. For each PR take the full head SHA from `gh pr view <n> --json headRefOid`, review exactly that, and check at the end whether it moved or was merged.\n\nPR #774 \"feat(assurance): bound cumulative objective execution time\" (`gh pr view 774`, `gh pr diff 774`; +341/−10): `cli/src/config.ts`, `cli/src/core/execution_tracking.ts`, `cli/src/core/run_turn.ts`, `cli/src/core/turn.ts`, `cli/src/doctor.ts`, `cli/src/index.ts`, `cli/src/types.ts`, `cli/test/p10_task_elapsed_budget.test.ts`, the P10 plan doc, `docs/protocol/RUN_RESULT_VERSIONS.json`, `docs/protocol/run-result-v1.schema.json`. Context: work package WP-P10-02 of `docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`. Already merged in this series: a cumulative inference-submission budget (PR #760: counter persisted with the objective, resume can only lower the ceiling, at the limit the turn ends `LIMIT_REACHED` with nothing retried) and an in-turn deadline timer (PR #762: `maxTurnMinutes` enforced while async work is in flight, reported `TIME_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED`). This PR bounds cumulative elapsed time across turns and resumes.\n Questions for #774: (1) What clock and what is counted: wall time while a turn is running only, or including idle time between turns/resumes? Is elapsed time persisted with the objective before/after each turn so a crash or a kill cannot reset it; can a resume raise the ceiling or reset the counter (it must only keep or lower); what happens to a legacy saved objective with no counter; is a clock jump (system time set backwards/forwards) handled (monotonic source within a process, wall clock across processes — say what the code does and what a backwards jump would do)? (2) At the limit: a defined non-success result (which execution/reason), nothing dispatched afterwards, never COMPLETED/VERIFIED; interaction with the in-turn deadline timer of #762 (two timers? which wins; is every timer cleared on all exits — the earlier review of #762 checked for stale timers firing into a later turn). (3) Who can configure it: flag/env/config; can a project `.env` raise it (the submission budget's key is in `PROJECT_ENV_KEYS` in `config.ts` — is this one, and do the docs say so?); min/default/max; invalid value fails closed. (4) Schema and ledgers: additive, earlier frozen versions untouched, `schema_version` policy followed; `cli/test/fixtures/protocol_v1_schema_samples.jsonl` regenerated if the sidecar schema changed (`node cli/scripts/gen_protocol_samples.mjs --check`) — PR #760 failed CI on exactly this. (5) The new test file registers the leak guard (`import \"./helpers/leak_guard.js\"`; `cli/test/leak_guard.test.ts` fails otherwise — PRs #760 and #762 both missed it). (6) Complexity gate: `runTurnImpl` is a listed critical function that must not grow in cyclomatic complexity or nesting; run from the worktree root `node cli/node_modules/tsx/dist/cli.mjs cli/scripts/check_critical_complexity.ts` and report its output. (7) Mutations (copy the source file aside and restore from the copy; do not use `git checkout` to undo): disable the admission check; reset the counter on resume — does `p10_task_elapsed_budget.test.ts` fail each time?\n\nPR #775 \"feat(goal): enforce optional PA-3 token budget cap\" (`gh pr view 775`, `gh pr diff 775`; +135/−5): `cli/src/batch.ts`, `cli/src/config.ts`, `cli/src/core/operation.ts`, `cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts`, `cli/src/core/operation_schema.ts`, `cli/src/goal.ts`, `cli/src/goal_command.ts`, `cli/src/types.ts`, `cli/test/goal_lifecycle.test.ts`, `docs/v1.3.0/PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md`. Context: plan unit PA-3 in `docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md` (goal lifecycle; \"a stale goal resumes paused; a model's 'done' does not complete it\"); PR #758 (merged) added pause-on-restart and rolled-up token usage reporting.\n Questions for #775: (1) What is capped (reported tokens, estimated tokens, both; per goal across its sub-operations?), when is the cap checked (before starting a unit? after each? can one unit overshoot by an unbounded amount), and what state results (PAUSED with a visible reason? BLOCKED?), never COMPLETE. (2) Can a model, a tool result or workspace content raise or remove the cap, or mark the goal complete past it; who may set it (operator flag/env/config vs project file); can a resume raise it. (3) Does a goal with no cap behave exactly as before (the cap is optional); schema change optional and backward compatible with state written before this PR. (4) `driveOperation` is a listed critical function in the complexity gate (must not grow): run the gate and report. `operation_runner.ts` was the site of a regression in PR #758 (`operation_entry_integrity.test.ts`): run that file. (5) Mutation: remove the cap check — does `goal_lifecycle.test.ts` fail? (6) Does the doc claim only what code and tests show?\n\nFor both, run at each PR's head, one file at a time: the PR's own test file(s); `leak_guard`; `protocol_parity`; `protocol_schema`; `run_json_contract`; `check_requirements`; for #774 also `p10_inference_submission_budget`, `turn_deadline_abort`; for #775 also `goal_lifecycle`, `goal_ledger_propagation`, `operation_entry_integrity`, `operation_schema`, `operation_runner_restart`; `cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p .`. For any failure check the same file on `origin/release/v1.3.0` and report only differences (`doctor.test.ts` fails 11 tests on this host on the base too; skip it).\n\nMandatory rules:\n- Do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. One throwaway worktree per PR: `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/rev774 <sha>` (and `rev775`); for each: `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules <wt>/cli/`; `mkdir -p <wt>/core/target/release && cp ~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui} <wt>/core/target/release/`. Remove both at the end (`git -C ~/nexus-code worktree remove --force <wt>`). No commits, pushes or GitHub comments.\n- Tests: `cd <wt>/cli && HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20`, foreground, one file at a time, timeout at most 9 minutes (the runner prints `ℹ pass` / `ℹ fail`). Never read the real ~/.nexus, /etc/nexus or ~/.config/nexus. No live inference, no network.\n- Stop every process you start by its own pid; never `pkill -f`. No background loops.\n- Shell is zsh (use `bash -c` for loops; `$PIPESTATUS` is empty in zsh); output passes through `rtk` (use `rtk proxy <cmd>` if it looks filtered).\n\nReport under 650 words, one section per PR: verdict (ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS / REQUEST CHANGES) at the exact full SHA; findings ranked with file:line, each marked confirmed-by-running or by-reading, blocking vs non-blocking; gate output; mutation results; test counts; what you did not check."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":729,"cache_read_input_tokens":793728,"output_tokens":2994,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":729,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2994,"cache_read_input_tokens":793728,"cache_creation_input_tokens":729,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":72