{"parentUuid":"5fccdbba-991a-4554-ac4c-ef69ab865b0a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMWuLCckfRYvaKw5nEnT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The six VR-2 follow-ups are implemented, committed and pushed. Opening the PR and sending it for independent review now."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1567,"cache_read_input_tokens":800183,"output_tokens":1948,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1567,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1948,"cache_read_input_tokens":800183,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1567,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1567},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChMWuKyyVxpDJSr7EMk16","requestRef":"8c6d5479-8212-4384-927d-fcd8d8c6f25d","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"daadb2bf-6fef-497c-87c4-27b88e759190","timestamp":"2026-11-24T09:28:22.325Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"daadb2bf-6fef-497c-87c4-27b88e759190","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMWuLCckfRYvaKw5nEnT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01W3tZNangnQ5RcjJeSGYpkT","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_vr2f.md","content":"The six findings left open by the second review of #756 (the ACP verification extension, `_nexus/verify`).\n\n## What changes\n\n1. **The verification base is pinned per workspace, not per session.** A client could commit weakened tests, open a new session on the same directory, and be judged against a base that already contained them. The first session on a canonical directory now pins `HEAD` for the life of the `nexus acp` process; later sessions on it, new or loaded, reuse that pin. At most 16 workspaces are remembered; past that, verification of a new workspace is refused. Nothing is evicted or pinned again.\n2. **The result names what was covered**: `workspace`, `base_pinned_commit` and `base_pinned_at` are in the `_nexus/verify` result. Adapter schema v4, with a ledger entry; v1 to v3 are byte-identical.\n3. **`_nexus/receipt/get` without an id returns turn receipts only**, as it did before the extension. A verification receipt is read by its id and is bound to its session.\n4. **Interlock tests**: no verification during a prompt or a stopping turn; no prompt during a verification; refusal in read-only mode; no receipt read from another live session on the same connection.\n5. **Shutdown bound**: while a verification is running, a signalled adapter waits at least the verify kill grace plus 5 s.\n6. **`_meta`** on `_nexus/verify` is accepted and never read, like on the other methods; `docs/ACP.md` says so.\n\n`docs/ACP.md` gains a `_nexus/verify` section (there was none): the client chooses the directory, the operator's verifier and deliverables are fixed at start-up and applied to it, the base is pinned per workspace until the process restarts, and the same-user limit of `docs/MCP_GUIDE.md` applies. One sentence in `docs/MCP_GUIDE.md` that said \"per session\" is corrected.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew `acp_verify_followups.test.ts` (8) and additions to `acp_review_fixes.test.ts` and `acp_stdio.test.ts`. Removing each of the following fails a test: the verify-during-prompt check, the per-workspace pin, the cap, the prompt-during-verify check, the receipt separation, the signal deadline.\n\nLocal, Node 24: `acp_verify_followups` 8/8, `acp_review_fixes` 9/9, `acp_validate` 15/15, `acp_schema` 7/7, `acp_mapping` 22/22, `acp_client_conformance` 2/2 (the recorded Zed and CodeCompanion sessions still replay), `acp_jsonrpc` 11/11, `verify_service` 10/10, `mcp_verify` 7/7, `leak_guard` 6/6. `tsc`, the schema generator's check, `check_invariants`, `check_doc_versions` and the complexity gate pass.\n\n**One test-timing change:** `acp_stdio.test.ts` waited 10 s for a real turn. Under load two of its nine tests timed out, and one of them timed out 6 of 6 on unchanged sources at the same load; a turn took about 4.8 s on a quieter host. The wait is now 45 s. The first review of #741 had flagged that deadline.\n\n## Decisions taken\n\n- A workspace with no commit at its first session keeps that refusal until the process restarts; otherwise \"commit, then open a new session\" would choose the base.\n- A failed `session/load` still uses a pin slot.\n- The three new fields are on the ACP result only; the shared service summary and the MCP tool's output are unchanged.\n\n## Not done\n\n- The shutdown bound mirrors `serve-mcp` (kill grace + 5 s) and does not cover the last stage of a kill at twice the grace.\n- Node 22 was not run locally.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1567,"cache_read_input_tokens":800183,"output_tokens":1948,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1567,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1948,"cache_read_input_tokens":800183,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1567,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1567},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":12637,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01W3tZNangnQ5RcjJeSGYpkT":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_vr2f.md","content":"The six findings left open by the second review of #756 (the ACP verification extension, `_nexus/verify`).\n\n## What changes\n\n1. **The verification base is pinned per workspace, not per session.** A client could commit weakened tests, open a new session on the same directory, and be judged against a base that already contained them. The first session on a canonical directory now pins `HEAD` for the life of the `nexus acp` process; later sessions on it, new or loaded, reuse that pin. At most 16 workspaces are remembered; past that, verification of a new workspace is refused. Nothing is evicted or pinned again.\n2. **The result names what was covered**: `workspace`, `base_pinned_commit` and `base_pinned_at` are in the `_nexus/verify` result. Adapter schema v4, with a ledger entry; v1 to v3 are byte-identical.\n3. **`_nexus/receipt/get` without an id returns turn receipts only**, as it did before the extension. A verification receipt is read by its id and is bound to its session.\n4. **Interlock tests**: no verification during a prompt or a stopping turn; no prompt during a verification; refusal in read-only mode; no receipt