{"parentUuid":"8aedaebd-9c10-4f87-8863-5469e3b93da8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMWwMgEPRweLXMXVJt7e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BCGX6HR1QcJuwrW1YWFPza","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Review PR #777 VR-2 follow-ups","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Independent security review of GitHub PR #777 in the repo at ~/nexus-code (`gh pr view 777`, `gh pr diff 777`), \"fix(acp): pin the verification base per workspace, name what was verified, keep turn receipts separate\", base `release/v1.3.0`. Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 777 --json headRefOid`, review exactly that, and check at the end whether it moved or was merged. Time-box: about 40 minutes; if you run short, give a verdict on what you covered and list the rest.\n\nContext: `nexus acp` is an Agent Client Protocol server over stdio for an UNTRUSTED client (`cli/src/acp_stdio.ts`, `cli/src/acp/{types,validate,mapping}.ts`). Its extension method `_nexus/verify` runs the operator-configured verifier on the session's workspace through the shared `VerifyService` (`cli/src/core/verify_service.ts`) and returns a verdict and a receipt id; receipts are read with `_nexus/receipt/get`. The PR body lists six changes; the design plan is `/home/mike/nexus-wt/_plans/VR2_PLAN.md`. The second review of the original PR (#756) is the source of the six findings: read its comment with `gh pr view 756 --comments` (the one beginning \"Second independent review at `f25030a3…`\").\n\nTry to break each claim, by running where practical (fake-sidecar/fake-service tests in the style of `cli/test/acp_verify_followups.test.ts` and `cli/test/acp_review_fixes.test.ts`; write probes as an extra untracked test file in `cli/test/` that you delete afterwards):\n1. Per-workspace base pin. Can a client still get a later base for the same directory: through a different spelling of the path (symlink, trailing slash, `..`, case, a bind-mount-like second path to the same directory — how is \"canonical\" computed, and is it the same canonical form the verification then uses as the worktree?); through `session/load` versus `session/new`; by exhausting the 16-slot cap with other directories (the stated behaviour is refusal for new workspaces, existing pins kept — confirm an existing pin survives and that hitting the cap cannot evict or re-pin); by making the first pin fail (a workspace with no commit, then committing: the PR says the refusal sticks until restart — confirm, and check whether a client can use that to permanently deny verification of a workspace for the life of the process: say so as a limit if yes); by racing two `session/new` on the same directory. Is the pin taken before any client-influenced git state could matter, and with which git command (hardened flags? could a repository-configured program run at pin time — `rev-parse` should not, confirm by reading `pinBase`)?\n2. Result fields `workspace`, `base_pinned_commit`, `base_pinned_at`: do they always describe what was actually verified (same canonical path and the same commit passed to the service), including when the verdict is BLOCKED or the service refuses? Schema v4: are `docs/protocol/acp-adapter-v1..v3.schema.json` byte-identical to the base branch (`git diff origin/release/v1.3.0 -- docs/protocol/acp-adapter-v[123].schema.json` must be empty), does the generator's check pass, does `initialize` advertise the right version, and do the recorded real-client fixtures still replay (`cli/test/acp_client_conformance.test.ts`)?\n3. Receipt separation: id-less `_nexus/receipt/get` returns only turn receipts in every ordering (verify before any turn; turn then verify; verify then turn); a verification receipt id from session A cannot be read from session B on the same connection, nor after session A is gone; forged/unknown ids.\n4. Interlocks: verify during a prompt, during `stopping`, prompt during verify, `$/cancel_request` of the verify request, `session/cancel` during a verify, connection close during a verify: no state is left that blocks the session forever, and nothing runs when refused. Mutate (copy the source aside, restore from the copy; never `git checkout` to undo): remove the verify-during-prompt check, the per-workspace pin reuse, and the id-less receipt filter; the test files must fail each time.\n5. Shutdown bound: read `shutdownGraceMs()` and its use; can the longer deadline be made to apply forever (a verification that never ends is bounded by the service watchdog — confirm), and does a signal with no verification running still exit within the original bound?\n6. The test-timing change (10 s → 45 s wait for a real turn in `cli/test/acp_stdio.test.ts`): is any assertion weakened besides the wait?\n7. Docs (`docs/ACP.md` `_nexus/verify` section, `docs/evidence/v1.3.0/VR2.md`, the one-sentence change in `docs/MCP_GUIDE.md`): claim only what code and tests show?\n\nRun at head, one file at a time: `acp_verify_followups`, `acp_review_fixes`, `acp_stdio` (allow it 9 minutes; real turns are slow under load), `acp_validate`, `acp_schema`, `acp_mapping`, `acp_client_conformance`, `acp_jsonrpc`, `verify_service`, `leak_guard`; `cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p .`; from the worktree root `node cli/scripts/gen_acp_schema.mjs --check` and `node cli/node_modules/tsx/dist/cli.mjs cli/scripts/check_critical_complexity.ts`. For any failure, check the same file on `origin/release/v1.3.0`.\n\nMandatory rules:\n- Do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/rev777 <full sha>`; `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/rev777/cli/`; `mkdir -p ~/nexus-wt/rev777/core/target/release && cp ~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui} ~/nexus-wt/rev777/core/target/release/`. At the end delete any probe file and run `git -C ~/nexus-code worktree remove --force ~/nexus-wt/rev777`. No commits, pushes or GitHub comments.\n- Tests: `cd ~/nexus-wt/rev777/cli && HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20`, foreground, one at a time (the runner prints `ℹ pass` / `ℹ fail`). Never read the real ~/.nexus, /etc/nexus or ~/.config/nexus. No live inference, no network.\n- Stop every process you start by its own pid; never `pkill -f`. No background loops.\n- Shell is zsh (use `bash -c` for loops; `$PIPESTATUS` is empty in zsh); output passes through `rtk` (use `rtk proxy <cmd>` if it looks filtered).\n\nReport under 600 words: verdict (ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS / REQUEST CHANGES) at the exact full SHA; findings ranked with file:line, each marked confirmed-by-running or by-reading, blocking vs non-blocking; mutation results; test counts; what you did not check."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2131,"cache_read_input_tokens":801750,"output_tokens":2629,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2131,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2629,"cache_read_input_tokens":801750,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2131,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2131},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":23876,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01BCGX6HR1QcJuwrW1YWFPza":{"description":"Review PR #777 VR-2 follow-ups","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Independent security review of GitHub PR #777 in the repo at ~/nexus-code (`gh pr view 777`, `gh pr diff 777`), \"fix(acp): pin the verification base per workspace, name what was verified, keep turn receipts separate\", base `release/v1.3.0`. Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 777 --json headRefOid`, review exactly that, and check at the end whether it moved or was merged. Time-box: about 40 minutes; if you run short, give a verdict on what you covered and list the rest.\n\nContext: `nexus acp` is an Agent Client Protocol server over stdio for an UNTRUSTED client (`cli/src/acp_stdio.ts`, `cli/src/acp/{types,validate,mapping}.ts`). Its extension method `_nexus/verify` runs the operator-configured verifier on the session's workspace through the shared `VerifyService` (`cli/src/core/verify_service.ts`) and returns a verdict and a receipt id; receipts are read with `_nexus/receipt/get`. The PR body lists six changes; the design plan is `/home/mike/nexus-wt/_plans/VR2_PLAN.md`. The second review of the original PR (#756) is the source of the six findings: read its comment with `gh pr view 756 --comments` (the one beginning \"Second independent review at `f25030a3…`\").\n\nTry to break each claim, by running where practical (fake-sidecar/fake-service tests in the style of `cli/test/acp_verify_followups.test.ts` and `cli/test/acp_review_fixes.test.ts`; write probes as an extra untracked test file in `cli/test/` that you delete afterwards):\n1. Per-workspace base pin. Can a client still get a later base for the same directory: through a different spelling of the path (symlink, trailing slash, `..`, case, a bind-mount-like second path to the same directory — how is \"canonical\" computed, and is it the same canonical form the verification then uses as the worktree?); through `session/load` versus `session/new`; by exhausting the 16-slot cap with other directories (the stated behaviour is refusal for new workspaces, existing pins kept — confirm an existing pin survives and that hitting the cap cannot evict or re-pin); by making the first pin fail (a workspace with no commit, then committing: the PR says the refusal sticks until restart — confirm, and check whether a client can use that to